ehousing'}, {'relevance': 0.004660873208194971, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>3-DGraphics'}, {'relevance': 0.003986736293882132, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.0026918179355561733, 'label': 'Science>Physics'}, {'relevance': 0.0025913650169968605, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ProgrammingLanguages'}, {'relevance': 0.002461665775626898, 'label': 'Science'}, {'relevance': 0.0011800369247794151, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.0010058105690404773, 'label': 'Science>Chemistry'}, {'relevance': 0.0005786877009086311, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>Search'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 2220, 'end': 37480}, 'sentences_idx_start': 0, 'sentences_idx_end': 8}, {'text': "So if you want to go into the details, just kind of look this up on the Internet and you should be able to find it easily. Obviously, there's lots of stuff in there. So I kind of try to give an overview today and maybe also go in a little bit more detail in certain aspects since there's not a lot of time to go through.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.0820825919508934, 'label': 'FineArt>Design'}, {'relevance': 0.020917633548378944, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>DesktopPublishing'}, {'relevance': 0.0058122421614825726, 'label': 'Automotive>AutoType>ConceptCars'}, {'relevance': 0.0056651439517736435, 'label': 'Home&Garden>HomeImprovement'}, {'relevance': 0.00459581334143877, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Industries>ConstructionIndustry'}, {'relevance': 0.004206586163491011, 'label': 'BooksAndLiterature>ArtAndPhotographyBooks'}, {'relevance': 0.0029858809430152178, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ContentProduction>Screenwriting'}, {'relevance': 0.0025867598596960306, 'label': 'RealEstate>IndustrialProperty'}, {'relevance': 0.002573629142716527, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>GamesAndPuzzles>RoleplayingGames'}, {'relevance': 0.002309685107320547, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>Sci-fiAndFantasy'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 37550, 'end': 58370}, 'sentences_idx_start': 9, 'sentences_idx_end': 11}, {'text': "Yeah, now I'm Microsoft Research, so this is basically all work that I did in the past and when I was at University of Cambridge. All right, so let's get started. Right, so let's start very easily.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.020455103367567062, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>DataStorageAndWarehousing'}, {'relevance': 0.007111000828444958, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Business>BusinessI.T.'}, {'relevance': 0.004025403875857592, 'label': 'Education>OnlineEducation'}, {'relevance': 0.003074112581089139, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>ITAndInternetSupport'}, {'relevance': 0.0012322411639615893, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Industries>InformationServicesIndustry'}, {'relevance': 0.0011653861729428172, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Industries>ManagementConsultingIndustry'}, {'relevance': 0.0009548676898702979, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ContentProduction'}, {'relevance': 0.0009263119427487254, 'label': 'Education>EducationalAssessment'}, {'relevance': 0.0008719100151211023, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Business>MarketingAndAdvertising'}, {'relevance': 0.0007633228087797761, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>InformationAndNetworkSecurity'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 60180, 'end': 76020}, 'sentences_idx_start': 12, 'sentences_idx_end': 14}, {'text': "Now, I'm actually not sure exactly what's kind of the background of the people who are watching, but in machine learning there's all these kind of subfield that emerged a few years ago which is called geometric deep learning, which is essentially looking at how to apply these kind of deep learning. Neural network architectures on data, living on all sorts of structures or geometries or spaces if you want. And this has a lot of application, especially in the life sciences.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.9858818054199219, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.47895118594169617, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.048507388681173325, 'label': 'Technology&Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.03339537978172302, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ProgrammingLanguages'}, {'relevance': 0.024122031405568123, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Robotics'}, {'relevance': 0.0023300934117287397, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>3-DGraphics'}, {'relevance': 0.002055342076346278, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Industries>BiotechAndBiomedicalIndustry'}, {'relevance': 0.0020442972891032696, 'label': 'Science'}, {'relevance': 0.001990863122045994, 'label': 'VideoGaming>VideoGameGenres>SimulationVideoGames'}, {'relevance': 0.0016628458397462964, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>InternetOfThings'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 76760, 'end': 109740}, 'sentences_idx_start': 15, 'sentences_idx_end': 17}, {'text': "And there's kind of been a lot of instances of this in kind of very famous publications, some of which you see here. But just to give some examples, for instance, if you have proteins or molecules or things like that, they usually represented as graphs. And you kind of have some data living on these graphs, like kind of the properties of certain atoms and so on.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.8168589472770691, 'label': 'Science>Chemistry'}, {'relevance': 0.24964582920074463, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>3-DGraphics'}, {'relevance': 0.1703464835882187, 'label': 'Science'}, {'relevance': 0.15475621819496155, 'label': 'Science>Physics'}, {'relevance': 0.12544122338294983, 'label': 'Science>BiologicalSciences'}, {'relevance': 0.01228381134569645, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.008496659807860851, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>GraphicsSoftware'}, {'relevance': 0.004292141646146774, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>DataStorageAndWarehousing'}, {'relevance': 0.004096514079719782, 'label': 'Science>SpaceAndAstronomy'}, {'relevance': 0.003165571251884103, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>Databases'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 109820, 'end': 131530}, 'sentences_idx_start': 18, 'sentences_idx_end': 20}, {'text': "So these kind of things and so far, these kind of spaces or these kind of problems, learning problems, if you want, they have been approached mostly kind of with a geometrical mindset, as the kind of name of this subfield also mentions. But something that I would argue is that geometry is not everything that you need and there's kind of other non geometrical aspects when you are in such a setting.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.23410306870937347, 'label': 'Science>Geography'}, {'relevance': 0.058549780398607254, 'label': 'Home&Garden>Landscaping'}, {'relevance': 0.032970130443573, 'label': 'FineArt>Design'}, {'relevance': 0.010122491046786308, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Industries>CivilEngineeringIndustry'}, {'relevance': 0.004396606702357531, 'label': 'Science>Geology'}, {'relevance': 0.004271234385669231, 'label': 'Science'}, {'relevance': 0.003900516778230667, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>3-DGraphics'}, {'relevance': 0.0028133203741163015, 'label': 'RealEstate>DevelopmentalSites'}, {'relevance': 0.0019558744970709085, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Industries>MechanicalAndIndustrialEngineeringIndustry'}, {'relevance': 0.001438296982087195, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ArtsAndCrafts>DrawingAndSketching'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 132380, 'end': 162960}, 'sentences_idx_start': 21, 'sentences_idx_end': 22}, {'text': "And this is kind of quite obvious once you realize that the spaces that kind of show up in the field and in many applications, they are very heterogeneous. So, as I mentioned, for instance, you could have graphs that could represent anything. In this case, it's the caffeine molecule that you see here on the left. And you want to have some models that predict certain properties of this molecule and so on. But for instance, you can have grids.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.35961437225341797, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>3-DGraphics'}, {'relevance': 0.1288720816373825, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.04692512005567551, 'label': 'Science>Chemistry'}, {'relevance': 0.021193573251366615, 'label': 'VideoGaming>VideoGameGenres>SimulationVideoGames'}, {'relevance': 0.01925414800643921, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ProgrammingLanguages'}, {'relevance': 0.011554674245417118, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>DataStorageAndWarehousing'}, {'relevance': 0.009745326824486256, 'label': 'Science>Physics'}, {'relevance': 0.008877192623913288, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>Databases'}, {'relevance': 0.007686822209507227, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>GraphicsSoftware'}, {'relevance': 0.002938478719443083, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>GamesAndPuzzles'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 164180, 'end': 189572}, 'sentences_idx_start': 23, 'sentences_idx_end': 27}, {'text': "And we see grids all the time and data living on grids. And I'm referring to images, videos, they are all kind of pixels living on a grid. And then you can have more sophisticated things. You could have some meshes, for instance. They're all over in computer graphics and then you could have some sort of manifold. So for instance, if you're doing maybe weather modeling or something, we live on a sphere, topologically speaking.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.9881309270858765, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>3-DGraphics'}, {'relevance': 0.6064722537994385, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>GraphicsSoftware'}, {'relevance': 0.07492318004369736, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.07286768406629562, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>PhotoEditingSoftware'}, {'relevance': 0.04968274384737015, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>ComputerAnimation'}, {'relevance': 0.03306204453110695, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>AugmentedReality'}, {'relevance': 0.025687653571367264, 'label': 'FineArt>DigitalArts'}, {'relevance': 0.012081686407327652, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ArtsAndCrafts>DrawingAndSketching'}, {'relevance': 0.007137238513678312, 'label': 'NewsAndPolitics>Weather'}, {'relevance': 0.006088705267757177, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>DataStorageAndWarehousing'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 189636, 'end': 217030}, 'sentences_idx_start': 28, 'sentences_idx_end': 33}, {'text': "So you might want to model your data as living on a sphere and so on. But nonetheless, even if these spaces are kind of geometrically, kind of heterogeneous, and some of them don't even have a geometrical structure in kind of a strict mathematical sense, they all have what's called a topological structure, which is kind of like kind of a weaker kind of structure, but it's kind of more general.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.06252521276473999, 'label': 'Science>Geography'}, {'relevance': 0.03368672356009483, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>Databases'}, {'relevance': 0.032430555671453476, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>DataStorageAndWarehousing'}, {'relevance': 0.0030304514802992344, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>3-DGraphics'}, {'relevance': 0.0012330478057265282, 'label': 'Home&Garden>Landscaping'}, {'relevance': 0.0006842776201665401, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Industries>LogisticsAndTransportationIndustry'}, {'relevance': 0.00047448440454900265, 'label': 'VideoGaming>VideoGameGenres>SimulationVideoGames'}, {'relevance': 0.000441951269749552, 'label': 'Science>BiologicalSciences'}, {'relevance': 0.0004005261289421469, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Economy>Commodities'}, {'relevance': 0.0003735578211490065, 'label': 'Science'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 217720, 'end': 244110}, 'sentences_idx_start': 34, 'sentences_idx_end': 35}, {'text': "And I'm going to talk a bit in a few seconds about what that means by in general. When you do kind of mathematical physics, you kind of have a ladder of structures where you kind of keep building on top and the more structure you have, the more sophisticated things you can do and so on.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.9966785907745361, 'label': 'Science>Physics'}, {'relevance': 0.05822059512138367, 'label': 'Science'}, {'relevance': 0.008907211013138294, 'label': 'Science>SpaceAndAstronomy'}, {'relevance': 0.002598842140287161, 'label': 'Science>Chemistry'}, {'relevance': 0.000521617941558361, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>3-DGraphics'}, {'relevance': 0.0005032590706832707, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.00041032719309441745, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Agnosticism'}, {'relevance': 0.0004068338021170348, 'label': "Style&Fashion>Men'sFashion>Men'sClothing>Men'sFormalWear"}, {'relevance': 0.00035966033465228975, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Astrology'}, {'relevance': 0.0003190356364939362, 'label': 'VideoGaming>VideoGameGenres>SimulationVideoGames'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 244560, 'end': 261024}, 'sentences_idx_start': 36, 'sentences_idx_end': 37}, {'text': 'And kind of at the base of this diagram just have sets, just kind of a collection of elements with no kind of extra structure and then you kind of keep going up in this ladder and you add stuff on top of sets and so on.', 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.03938765451312065, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ArtsAndCrafts>DrawingAndSketching'}, {'relevance': 0.01938597857952118, 'label': 'VideoGaming>VideoGameGenres>PuzzleVideoGames'}, {'relevance': 0.014058392494916916, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>3-DGraphics'}, {'relevance': 0.008529828861355782, 'label': 'FineArt>Design'}, {'relevance': 0.008466777391731739, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>GamesAndPuzzles'}, {'relevance': 0.00286259688436985, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>DataStorageAndWarehousing'}, {'relevance': 0.002576621249318123, 'label': 'Science>Geography'}, {'relevance': 0.002262063091620803, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>GamesAndPuzzles>BoardGamesAndPuzzles'}, {'relevance': 0.0010406445944681764, 'label': 'VideoGaming>VideoGameGenres>StrategyVideoGames'}, {'relevance': 0.0008945615263655782, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>Databases'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 261062, 'end': 275510}, 'sentences_idx_start': 38, 'sentences_idx_end': 38}, {'text': "And as I was saying, kind of most of the work is kind of focused on maybe the top levels of this hierarchy, but it's kind of topological level, which are kind of the weakest kind of level you can add on top of sets has kind of been neglected to a large extent. And part of what I've been doing in my PhD thesis was essentially looking at these kind of learning problems on these kind of spaces from a more topological perspective and kind of try to fill in these blanks.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.005024974700063467, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>Databases'}, {'relevance': 0.0049570705741643906, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ProgrammingLanguages'}, {'relevance': 0.003821788588538766, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>DataStorageAndWarehousing'}, {'relevance': 0.002163846278563142, 'label': 'Science'}, {'relevance': 0.0015078404685482383, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.0007647622842341661, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>GamesAndPuzzles'}, {'relevance': 0.0006573685677722096, 'label': 'Science>Chemistry'}, {'relevance': 0.0004750872030854225, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.0004509422869887203, 'label': 'Education>EducationalAssessment'}, {'relevance': 0.0003891719679813832, 'label': 'Science>Genetics'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 275880, 'end': 305040}, 'sentences_idx_start': 39, 'sentences_idx_end': 40}, {'text': "So this is kind of the overview, okay, so if we are to adopt this topological perspective, what would that actually mean or how would that look like? I guess it could look in different ways, but in what I've done, in my cases, it looks kind of like this. So we have horizontally, we kind of have a space that could be anything. This is just kind of an abstract space.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.013631480745971203, 'label': 'Science>Geography'}, {'relevance': 0.0016253561479970813, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>3-DGraphics'}, {'relevance': 0.0003761642728932202, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>VirtualReality'}, {'relevance': 0.000210305952350609, 'label': 'Home&Garden>Landscaping'}, {'relevance': 0.00020857561321463436, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Industries>LogisticsAndTransportationIndustry'}, {'relevance': 0.00017970883345697075, 'label': 'Science>Geology'}, {'relevance': 0.00016793048416730016, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ArtsAndCrafts>DrawingAndSketching'}, {'relevance': 0.00015846129099372774, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>DataStorageAndWarehousing'}, {'relevance': 0.00014171344810165465, 'label': 'NewsAndPolitics>Politics>WarAndConflicts'}, {'relevance': 0.00014034300693310797, 'label': 'Automotive>AutoBodyStyles>Sedan'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 305780, 'end': 328196}, 'sentences_idx_start': 41, 'sentences_idx_end': 44}, {'text': "It could be a grid or things like we've seen in the previous example and kind of vertically attached to the regions of this space. We have data. So data is kind of this vertical component and you kind of see these flags kind of being kind of anchored in these regions. So that kind of signifies you have some data that's kind of associated with that region. So that's kind of the high level perspective and I'm going to make that a bit more concrete a bit later.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.9951169490814209, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>DataStorageAndWarehousing'}, {'relevance': 0.9349443912506104, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>Databases'}, {'relevance': 0.01349799707531929, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Business>BusinessI.T.'}, {'relevance': 0.0037919473834335804, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications'}, {'relevance': 0.00278197112493217, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>CloudComputing'}, {'relevance': 0.002326702931895852, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Business>Logistics'}, {'relevance': 0.0008553984225727618, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Industries>InformationServicesIndustry'}, {'relevance': 0.0008073358912952244, 'label': 'Science>Geography'}, {'relevance': 0.000761733332183212, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>3-DGraphics'}, {'relevance': 0.0006611059070564806, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerNetworking'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 328378, 'end': 357890}, 'sentences_idx_start': 45, 'sentences_idx_end': 49}, {'text': "And there's kind of two essential things about this picture. A first thing is locality. So the data is attached to some regions of this space, this topological space, and in that sense it's local, so it's kind of associated with the region. And maybe to give a concrete example, if you kind of have a temperature sensor somewhere in space, right, you could think of whatever that sensor is measuring is kind of a property of kind of the immediate surrounding around that sensor.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.49643924832344055, 'label': 'Science>Geography'}, {'relevance': 0.22683513164520264, 'label': 'NewsAndPolitics>Weather'}, {'relevance': 0.006391415372490883, 'label': 'Science>SpaceAndAstronomy'}, {'relevance': 0.006284982897341251, 'label': 'Science>Environment'}, {'relevance': 0.002461519557982683, 'label': 'Science>Geology'}, {'relevance': 0.001965195406228304, 'label': 'Travel>TravelLocations>PolarTravel'}, {'relevance': 0.0017751777777448297, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>DataStorageAndWarehousing'}, {'relevance': 0.0016405415954068303, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>InternetOfThings'}, {'relevance': 0.001406755531206727, 'label': 'RealEstate>DevelopmentalSites'}, {'relevance': 0.0014060522662475705, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerNetworking'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 358340, 'end': 391336}, 'sentences_idx_start': 50, 'sentences_idx_end': 53}, {'text': "So it's kind of describing some property of a region in space. So that'll be kind of a concrete example. And another kind of axiom that we're starting with is that the space has structure. So the space has kind of, it's kind of made up of various regions and these regions intersect in various ways and that implicitly also makes our data structured because the data is attached to these regions. So there is kind of some structure in the data.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.9310494065284729, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>Databases'}, {'relevance': 0.8967239856719971, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>DataStorageAndWarehousing'}, {'relevance': 0.00526683172211051, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>3-DGraphics'}, {'relevance': 0.0018667413387447596, 'label': 'Science>Geography'}, {'relevance': 0.0013175210915505886, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Business>BusinessI.T.'}, {'relevance': 0.0012170537374913692, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ProgrammingLanguages'}, {'relevance': 0.0010603165719658136, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications'}, {'relevance': 0.001011137617751956, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.0009904323378577828, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerNetworking'}, {'relevance': 0.0005092412466183305, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>GenealogyAndAncestry'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 391368, 'end': 424390}, 'sentences_idx_start': 54, 'sentences_idx_end': 58}, {'text': "All right, so that's kind of the picture and actually many of these things relate to category theory. I'm not going to go in depth into this because it's kind of sophisticated and I'm not an expert myself in category theory, but kind of the high level here is that category theory is kind of a nice way.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.009609665721654892, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>Databases'}, {'relevance': 0.002391130430623889, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>DataStorageAndWarehousing'}, {'relevance': 0.0019357583951205015, 'label': 'Science'}, {'relevance': 0.0003534409333951771, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ProgrammingLanguages'}, {'relevance': 0.0002802270173560828, 'label': 'FineArt>Design'}, {'relevance': 0.0002773542364593595, 'label': 'Science>Physics'}, {'relevance': 0.0002137183619197458, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.00020707437943201512, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ParanormalPhenomena'}, {'relevance': 0.00019522351794876158, 'label': 'Science>Geography'}, {'relevance': 0.00016890540427993983, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 425800, 'end': 444540}, 'sentences_idx_start': 59, 'sentences_idx_end': 60}, {'text': 'To translate between different structure in mathematics and kind of discuss about properties of certain kinds of objects and translate that to some different kinds of objects and find all these kind of relations and connections. And a concrete example is, for instance, if you want to study some manifolds, some surfaces, you could associate some groups to these surfaces and then any sorts of relations between these kind of surfaces, also translating some relations about these groups or some other algebraic structures.', 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.8104699850082397, 'label': 'Science>Physics'}, {'relevance': 0.04993866756558418, 'label': 'Science>Chemistry'}, {'relevance': 0.011546562425792217, 'label': 'Science'}, {'relevance': 0.004628206603229046, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.003199162194505334, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ProgrammingLanguages'}, {'relevance': 0.0025134114548563957, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>3-DGraphics'}, {'relevance': 0.001220452832058072, 'label': 'Science>SpaceAndAstronomy'}, {'relevance': 0.0005839259829372168, 'label': 'Science>BiologicalSciences'}, {'relevance': 0.000402025441871956, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Industries>MetalsIndustry'}, {'relevance': 0.0003451808006502688, 'label': 'Science>Genetics'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 444610, 'end': 474096}, 'sentences_idx_start': 61, 'sentences_idx_end': 62}, {'text': "So you could study these manifolds by doing algebra instead of doing geometry or topology or something else. So also in this case, it's kind of manifesting the fact that we kind of translate these from spaces to data. So kind of because we associate the regions in a space, certain kinds of data, this is kind of how this translation manifests in what I've just described in the previous picture.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.12436794489622116, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>DataStorageAndWarehousing'}, {'relevance': 0.09082282334566116, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>Databases'}, {'relevance': 0.07266851514577866, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>3-DGraphics'}, {'relevance': 0.007173767313361168, 'label': 'Science>Physics'}, {'relevance': 0.002966552507132292, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.0024392735213041306, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ProgrammingLanguages'}, {'relevance': 0.0023793436121195555, 'label': 'Science>Geography'}, {'relevance': 0.0017244484042748809, 'label': 'Science>Chemistry'}, {'relevance': 0.0007981235394254327, 'label': 'Science>SpaceAndAstronomy'}, {'relevance': 0.0006362745771184564, 'label': 'Science'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 474208, 'end': 497192}, 'sentences_idx_start': 63, 'sentences_idx_end': 65}, {'text': "So you could think of this as some sort of translation or mapping from spaces and regions in that space to kind of data attached to that space. But yeah, I'm not going to go in a lot of detail into this, but just kind of to keep in the back of your mind that there's this stuff lurking in the background. All right, so I promise this is the only math definition I'm giving in this talk and then I'll stop.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.26133015751838684, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>DataStorageAndWarehousing'}, {'relevance': 0.19387920200824738, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>Databases'}, {'relevance': 0.01751510426402092, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>3-DGraphics'}, {'relevance': 0.01449200976639986, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.010651882737874985, 'label': 'Science>Physics'}, {'relevance': 0.008407708257436752, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ProgrammingLanguages'}, {'relevance': 0.001706162584014237, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerNetworking'}, {'relevance': 0.0008758573094382882, 'label': 'Science'}, {'relevance': 0.0007857594755478203, 'label': 'Science>Geography'}, {'relevance': 0.0007349961088038981, 'label': 'VideoGaming>VideoGameGenres>SimulationVideoGames'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 497256, 'end': 523910}, 'sentences_idx_start': 66, 'sentences_idx_end': 68}, {'text': "But just because I'm mentioning topological spaces quite often, I just wanted to kind of give this axiomatic definition, which might sound sophisticated, but I have a picture at the end and hopefully it'll be clear what is it. So it's just a set. As I was saying, we start with sets and we put stuff on top, right? So you start with a set and then you also have a collection of subsets of this set called the open sets that need to satisfy certain axioms.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.0015166143421083689, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>3-DGraphics'}, {'relevance': 0.0013366331113502383, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>Databases'}, {'relevance': 0.00123247888404876, 'label': 'Science>Geography'}, {'relevance': 0.0011190616060048342, 'label': 'Science>Chemistry'}, {'relevance': 0.0007363759214058518, 'label': 'Science>Physics'}, {'relevance': 0.0005866792635060847, 'label': 'Science>BiologicalSciences'}, {'relevance': 0.0005745928501710296, 'label': 'VideoGaming>VideoGameGenres>PuzzleVideoGames'}, {'relevance': 0.0004693170776590705, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>DataStorageAndWarehousing'}, {'relevance': 0.0003236619522795081, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>VirtualReality'}, {'relevance': 0.00021879545238334686, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Christianity'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 524600, 'end': 553448}, 'sentences_idx_start': 69, 'sentences_idx_end': 72}, {'text': "So you could think of these open sets as kind of regions of this space, very informally speaking. So something that kind of has to be satisfied is that, well, the empty set and the set itself need to be open set. So in some sense, you could think of this as saying the set itself is a region of that space very informally, which it's kind of, let's say, obvious. And then there's some kind of constraints about intersecting and taking units of this region.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.12660358846187592, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>Databases'}, {'relevance': 0.008891595527529716, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>DataStorageAndWarehousing'}, {'relevance': 0.0006624350789934397, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ProgrammingLanguages'}, {'relevance': 0.0006539585301652551, 'label': 'Science>Genetics'}, {'relevance': 0.0003249261644668877, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>GamesAndPuzzles>CardGames'}, {'relevance': 0.00019742318545468152, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>GamesAndPuzzles>BoardGamesAndPuzzles'}, {'relevance': 0.00019226949370931834, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>OperatingSystems'}, {'relevance': 0.0001919207425089553, 'label': 'Automotive>AutoBodyStyles>Sedan'}, {'relevance': 0.00017522551934234798, 'label': 'Home&Garden>InteriorDecorating'}, {'relevance': 0.00017336633754894137, 'label': 'Education>EducationalAssessment'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 553464, 'end': 586484}, 'sentences_idx_start': 73, 'sentences_idx_end': 76}, {'text': "So if we take the intersection of two regions, we should get another one of these regions. And if we take a union of these regions, we should get another region. And there are some constraints again, like, okay, how big these intersections should be. There should be finite intersections, but you could have infinite unions. But that's a technicality and we can just skip anyways. But to see a picture so on the left, you just see the set x itself.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.05895163491368294, 'label': 'Science>Geography'}, {'relevance': 0.0018995048012584448, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>Databases'}, {'relevance': 0.0013696450041607022, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>GenealogyAndAncestry'}, {'relevance': 0.00044975828495807946, 'label': 'Home&Garden>Landscaping'}, {'relevance': 0.00041224362212233245, 'label': 'RealEstate>DevelopmentalSites'}, {'relevance': 0.0003474938857834786, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Industries>LogisticsAndTransportationIndustry'}, {'relevance': 0.00033862495911307633, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>DataStorageAndWarehousing'}, {'relevance': 0.0002528731420170516, 'label': 'EventsAndAttractions>Parks&Nature'}, {'relevance': 0.00023593260266352445, 'label': 'Science>Geology'}, {'relevance': 0.00022169860312715173, 'label': 'Science>Genetics'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 586532, 'end': 615984}, 'sentences_idx_start': 77, 'sentences_idx_end': 82}, {'text': "And here I've put like a potential neighborhood structure or kind of like open set structure on this space. So we have an open set U, another open set V. By this axiom, their intersection should also be an open set. So you see this intersection in the middle being another open set, and then the set itself is another open set. So it's just kind of splitting stuff into regions, kind of. You could think of it like that.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.05890941247344017, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>Databases'}, {'relevance': 0.012880348600447178, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>DataStorageAndWarehousing'}, {'relevance': 0.00082754110917449, 'label': 'Home&Garden>Landscaping'}, {'relevance': 0.000746027217246592, 'label': 'Science>Geography'}, {'relevance': 0.0005677129956893623, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>3-DGraphics'}, {'relevance': 0.00038260783185251057, 'label': 'VideoGaming>VideoGameGenres>PuzzleVideoGames'}, {'relevance': 0.0003490949748083949, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerNetworking'}, {'relevance': 0.0003460819716565311, 'label': 'Home&Garden>Remodeling&Construction'}, {'relevance': 0.0002761778887361288, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>GamesAndPuzzles>BoardGamesAndPuzzles'}, {'relevance': 0.0002619082515593618, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>MedicalTests'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 616102, 'end': 639290}, 'sentences_idx_start': 83, 'sentences_idx_end': 88}, {'text': "All right, so this is a topological space, and now let's add data, right? So we mentioned that we have data and then we have a space, and then we add data on top. So so far we've seen how a topological space looks like. Now let's add this kind of vertical stuff, these flags that you saw before. We just put some data on top of these regions.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.06235630437731743, 'label': 'Science>Geography'}, {'relevance': 0.05702061206102371, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>DataStorageAndWarehousing'}, {'relevance': 0.033496104180812836, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>Databases'}, {'relevance': 0.010896077379584312, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>3-DGraphics'}, {'relevance': 0.0011680007446557283, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Industries>LogisticsAndTransportationIndustry'}, {'relevance': 0.0009631403372623026, 'label': 'NewsAndPolitics>Weather'}, {'relevance': 0.0006426481413654983, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerNetworking'}, {'relevance': 0.0005864000413566828, 'label': 'Home&Garden>Landscaping'}, {'relevance': 0.0004849914403166622, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>VirtualReality'}, {'relevance': 0.0004703242739196867, 'label': 'VideoGaming>VideoGameGenres>SimulationVideoGames'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 640160, 'end': 662960}, 'sentences_idx_start': 89, 'sentences_idx_end': 93}, {'text': 'And if we put data on all the regions of the space, on all the open sets, we get these structures that in categories here, like in algebraic topology, also geometry, they are called presheaves, which sounds very fancy, but all is just kind of a definition of what I was already describing. Essentially, you have some data for each region. For instance, for region U, you have this f of U, which is kind of the data attached to region U.', 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.7015380859375, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>Databases'}, {'relevance': 0.580570638179779, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>DataStorageAndWarehousing'}, {'relevance': 0.004840174689888954, 'label': 'Science>Geography'}, {'relevance': 0.003125052200630307, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>3-DGraphics'}, {'relevance': 0.0019295444944873452, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerNetworking'}, {'relevance': 0.0006991755217313766, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ProgrammingLanguages'}, {'relevance': 0.000672458263579756, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.0005161804729141295, 'label': 'Science>Chemistry'}, {'relevance': 0.0005038302624598145, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>GenealogyAndAncestry'}, {'relevance': 0.0004920519422739744, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Business>Logistics'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 663460, 'end': 696668}, 'sentences_idx_start': 94, 'sentences_idx_end': 96}, {'text': "So you could think of f of U, some set with describing the data that lives there in that region. But there's also an extra thing. You have some sort of maps going between these kind of pieces of data, and these are called restriction maps. And why is that? They provide you a way to kind of zoom in if you want, right? Like you have the data attached to the whole set x, and then you could think, okay, how do I take this data?", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.8261863589286804, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>DataStorageAndWarehousing'}, {'relevance': 0.7787872552871704, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>Databases'}, {'relevance': 0.017235692590475082, 'label': 'Science>Geography'}, {'relevance': 0.002570429118350148, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>3-DGraphics'}, {'relevance': 0.0013742592418566346, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerNetworking'}, {'relevance': 0.0010183360427618027, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Industries>LogisticsAndTransportationIndustry'}, {'relevance': 0.0009033521055243909, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>GenealogyAndAncestry'}, {'relevance': 0.0008200136944651604, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Business>Logistics'}, {'relevance': 0.0007910237181931734, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications'}, {'relevance': 0.0005160477012395859, 'label': 'Automotive>AutoTechnology>AutoNavigationSystems'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 696754, 'end': 726676}, 'sentences_idx_start': 97, 'sentences_idx_end': 102}, {'text': "How do I go from this data to data on a smaller region on x? So it's kind of a way to zoom in on that data, essentially. And I'm going to show some example in a second. So these are called pre sheaves. And just to see an example, our space here is kind of one of the simplest kind of space you could think of. It's just 1D or horizontal line, right? Just the real line.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.8056879043579102, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>DataStorageAndWarehousing'}, {'relevance': 0.43003180623054504, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>Databases'}, {'relevance': 0.09973106533288956, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>3-DGraphics'}, {'relevance': 0.0016144741093739867, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>PhotoEditingSoftware'}, {'relevance': 0.0013643910642713308, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications'}, {'relevance': 0.0011877334909513593, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>DigitalAudio'}, {'relevance': 0.001183912856504321, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>GraphicsSoftware'}, {'relevance': 0.0011384820099920034, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerPeripherals'}, {'relevance': 0.001125092850998044, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.0006194857996888459, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>AugmentedReality'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 726778, 'end': 752450}, 'sentences_idx_start': 103, 'sentences_idx_end': 109}, {'text': "And then you have some regions which are just given by open intervals on the real line. And then some pieces of data could be functions like continuous functions on those regions. So here's some sample data on this first interval. Here's another function on the second interval. Here's some data on this third interval. And actually in this case, it happens that all these functions agree on the overlap.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.2697664797306061, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>DataStorageAndWarehousing'}, {'relevance': 0.18814705312252045, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>Databases'}, {'relevance': 0.00207518576644361, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>3-DGraphics'}, {'relevance': 0.0011864032130688429, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>MedicalTests'}, {'relevance': 0.0006788648897781968, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerNetworking'}, {'relevance': 0.0005077267996966839, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>GenealogyAndAncestry'}, {'relevance': 0.0004943197127431631, 'label': 'Science>Geography'}, {'relevance': 0.00040936272125691175, 'label': 'Education>EducationalAssessment>StandardizedTesting'}, {'relevance': 0.0003941229952033609, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>DigitalAudio'}, {'relevance': 0.00038186158053576946, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>PhotoEditingSoftware'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 752900, 'end': 781396}, 'sentences_idx_start': 110, 'sentences_idx_end': 115}, {'text': "So where these regions overlap, they take the same values and we can actually glue them together in a single function over the entire region. So this is just an example of a preshief and it's called the preshift of continuous functions. So our data in this case is continuous functions and the space is just the realign and we put these functions on top of the realign.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.6355916857719421, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>DataStorageAndWarehousing'}, {'relevance': 0.47744807600975037, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>Databases'}, {'relevance': 0.008793826214969158, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>3-DGraphics'}, {'relevance': 0.0008270866819657385, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>MedicalTests'}, {'relevance': 0.0007768213399685919, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ProgrammingLanguages'}, {'relevance': 0.0007022708305157721, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerNetworking'}, {'relevance': 0.0005758771440014243, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>DigitalAudio'}, {'relevance': 0.0004325234331190586, 'label': 'Science>Physics'}, {'relevance': 0.00037858972791582346, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>PhotoEditingSoftware'}, {'relevance': 0.00034193971077911556, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerPeripherals'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 781428, 'end': 805920}, 'sentences_idx_start': 116, 'sentences_idx_end': 118}, {'text': "But it turns out because of this kind of special property, that we can kind of glue data and we uniquely get some other piece of data, right? We can take these three pieces. It's just exactly like a puzzle, right? We put these things together and we get a fourth thing, which is kind of a single function where we just overlap these functions, right? And these presheaves that satisfy these kind of properties where you can kind of glue them to get a unique piece of data.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.8313988447189331, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>Databases'}, {'relevance': 0.6990616917610168, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>DataStorageAndWarehousing'}, {'relevance': 0.0017956327646970749, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ProgrammingLanguages'}, {'relevance': 0.0006455714465118945, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>3-DGraphics'}, {'relevance': 0.0005613436223939061, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Business>BusinessI.T.'}, {'relevance': 0.0005242616753093898, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>MedicalTests'}, {'relevance': 0.0004985741688869894, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.00047867605462670326, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>GenealogyAndAncestry'}, {'relevance': 0.00029534430359490216, 'label': 'VideoGaming>VideoGameGenres>PuzzleVideoGames'}, {'relevance': 0.00026144194998778403, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 806260, 'end': 836024}, 'sentences_idx_start': 119, 'sentences_idx_end': 123}, {'text': "They are called sheaves and basically the preshave of continuous functions is actually a sheep. So this is kind of a way to formalize data attached to these things. It's going to get less technical in a second. So just to give more examples. So for instance, in this way we could describe data on a sphere. And let's say if this data is just some vector field on a sphere.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.7674295902252197, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>Databases'}, {'relevance': 0.6723694205284119, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>DataStorageAndWarehousing'}, {'relevance': 0.03323011472821236, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ProgrammingLanguages'}, {'relevance': 0.005969310645014048, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.0021587538067251444, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications'}, {'relevance': 0.0013276214012876153, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Business>BusinessI.T.'}, {'relevance': 0.0008137879776768386, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>3-DGraphics'}, {'relevance': 0.00028393883258104324, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerNetworking'}, {'relevance': 0.0002649823436513543, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerPeripherals'}, {'relevance': 0.0002530764904804528, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>OperatingSystems'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 836142, 'end': 862364}, 'sentences_idx_start': 124, 'sentences_idx_end': 129}, {'text': "So let's say if this is Earth, right, this could be some wind vector field, right? Like if we do weather modeling or something, you just have a vector field describing the wind on the surface of Earth, right?", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.994616687297821, 'label': 'NewsAndPolitics>Weather'}, {'relevance': 0.0017934810603037477, 'label': 'Travel>TravelLocations>PolarTravel'}, {'relevance': 0.0007737704436294734, 'label': 'Science>Environment'}, {'relevance': 0.0006021311273798347, 'label': 'Science>SpaceAndAstronomy'}, {'relevance': 0.00025225814897567034, 'label': 'Pets>Birds'}, {'relevance': 0.00020557963580358773, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Astrology'}, {'relevance': 0.00015971976972650737, 'label': 'Sports>Sailing'}, {'relevance': 0.00015924971376080066, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.00014067273878026754, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerNetworking'}, {'relevance': 0.00013574633339885622, 'label': 'Science>Geography'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 862412, 'end': 874790}, 'sentences_idx_start': 130, 'sentences_idx_end': 131}, {'text': 'And you might want to do some machine learning on top of this, where this kind of vector field has a sheet structure, and you could think of it as a sheath, because if you have some vector field on the red region, a vector field on the yellow region, I can kind of glue them together uniquely if they overlap. If they agree on the overlap and we get the vector field on this bigger region.', 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.058252524584531784, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>3-DGraphics'}, {'relevance': 0.003608931787312031, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.0032035429030656815, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Robotics'}, {'relevance': 0.0027953851968050003, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>AugmentedReality'}, {'relevance': 0.0015017082914710045, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>DataStorageAndWarehousing'}, {'relevance': 0.0009378036484122276, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.000818727829027921, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>VirtualReality'}, {'relevance': 0.000743210082873702, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ProgrammingLanguages'}, {'relevance': 0.000592174066696316, 'label': 'Science>Physics'}, {'relevance': 0.00044747343054041266, 'label': 'Automotive>AutoTechnology>AutoNavigationSystems'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 875160, 'end': 896140}, 'sentences_idx_start': 132, 'sentences_idx_end': 133}, {'text': "But something that's quite nice is that even if we have a very different kind of space namely a graph which is very different from a sphere in all points of view, we can still apply the exact same kind of axioms and terminology and kind of definitions and we can have a sheath of our graph.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.027489710599184036, 'label': 'Science>Geography'}, {'relevance': 0.011745424941182137, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>3-DGraphics'}, {'relevance': 0.0007548946887254715, 'label': 'Science>BiologicalSciences'}, {'relevance': 0.000694906571879983, 'label': 'Science>Physics'}, {'relevance': 0.0005094603984616697, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>VirtualReality'}, {'relevance': 0.0004691958602052182, 'label': 'Science>SpaceAndAstronomy'}, {'relevance': 0.00036738862399943173, 'label': 'Science>Geology'}, {'relevance': 0.0003195382305420935, 'label': 'Science>Chemistry'}, {'relevance': 0.0002987947955261916, 'label': 'Science>Genetics'}, {'relevance': 0.00028683821437880397, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Economy>Commodities'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 896960, 'end': 915244}, 'sentences_idx_start': 134, 'sentences_idx_end': 134}, {'text': "So in this way we could have, for instance, some features associated to the nodes of the graph, some features associated with the edges of the graph, and there's another node which has its own features and this is actually the exact same thing we have in graph machine learning. So this is quite nice.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.015652896836400032, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>3-DGraphics'}, {'relevance': 0.014264543540775776, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>Databases'}, {'relevance': 0.007400523405522108, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ProgrammingLanguages'}, {'relevance': 0.005441214889287949, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>DataStorageAndWarehousing'}, {'relevance': 0.003763046581298113, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.002560386201366782, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.0005830483860336244, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>GenealogyAndAncestry'}, {'relevance': 0.0005441383109427989, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Robotics'}, {'relevance': 0.0004449248663149774, 'label': 'Science>Geography'}, {'relevance': 0.00030034477822482586, 'label': 'Science>Genetics'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 915292, 'end': 932744}, 'sentences_idx_start': 135, 'sentences_idx_end': 136}, {'text': "What this kind of topological perspective allows us to do is we kind of have a unified way of thinking, if you want, about very kind of heterogeneous spaces and we can model on all of them data attached to them by using this kind of sheet terminology and other ways as well. But I'm not going into that in this talk. All right, so this is kind of an overview of what I've been doing in my thesis.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.1915331333875656, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>DataStorageAndWarehousing'}, {'relevance': 0.11455144733190536, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>Databases'}, {'relevance': 0.07416804134845734, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>3-DGraphics'}, {'relevance': 0.009039035998284817, 'label': 'Science>Geography'}, {'relevance': 0.0025359662249684334, 'label': 'VideoGaming>VideoGameGenres>SimulationVideoGames'}, {'relevance': 0.0011395512847229838, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>VirtualReality'}, {'relevance': 0.0011019207304343581, 'label': 'VideoGaming>VideoGameGenres>PuzzleVideoGames'}, {'relevance': 0.0009887362830340862, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Industries>LogisticsAndTransportationIndustry'}, {'relevance': 0.000939049175940454, 'label': 'Home&Garden>Landscaping'}, {'relevance': 0.0007165686110965908, 'label': 'Science>Physics'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 932782, 'end': 958320}, 'sentences_idx_start': 137, 'sentences_idx_end': 139}, {'text': "And just to kind of dive a bit deeper into this, I just wanted to go into one paper that we did at Europe last year. Yeah. So this was last year on what's called shift diffusion. So essentially, how can we use what I've just described to do some useful stuff when doing machine learning on graphs, all right? And this was a collaboration with Francesco de Giovanni ben Chamberlain pietro Leo, my advisor and Michael Bronstein. Okay?", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.05408170446753502, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.007094943430274725, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ProgrammingLanguages'}, {'relevance': 0.0063303071074187756, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>DataStorageAndWarehousing'}, {'relevance': 0.0062012686394155025, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.00585112813860178, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>Databases'}, {'relevance': 0.004053236450999975, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>3-DGraphics'}, {'relevance': 0.0005032580811530352, 'label': 'Science'}, {'relevance': 0.0004906096728518605, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>Search'}, {'relevance': 0.00038986580329947174, 'label': 'Science>Physics'}, {'relevance': 0.0003809049667324871, 'label': 'Technology&Computing'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 958980, 'end': 993932}, 'sentences_idx_start': 140, 'sentences_idx_end': 145}, {'text': 'So before I dive into this, I just want to give some background in case people are not familiar with this. So the kind of favorite architecture of people doing machine learning on graphs these days are these things called graph neural networks, which are actually very simple kind of models. So in the setting you have some features. So each node in your graph will have some features. This is what this h vector here denotes.', 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.08204817771911621, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.06517364084720612, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ProgrammingLanguages'}, {'relevance': 0.06027378886938095, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.04694317281246185, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>3-DGraphics'}, {'relevance': 0.01189849991351366, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>Databases'}, {'relevance': 0.004284567199647427, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>DataStorageAndWarehousing'}, {'relevance': 0.0026192613877356052, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Robotics'}, {'relevance': 0.0015317549696192145, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>GraphicsSoftware'}, {'relevance': 0.0007911970606073737, 'label': 'VideoGaming>VideoGameGenres>SimulationVideoGames'}, {'relevance': 0.0004583943809848279, 'label': 'Technology&Computing'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 993986, 'end': 1025936}, 'sentences_idx_start': 146, 'sentences_idx_end': 150}, {'text': "So it's the vector h associated with node A at layer or time t, whatever. So you have some features for each of these nodes and what you're doing each of if you're at a certain node, you want to kind of compute a new representation or new features for this node at the next layer. So essentially are learning representations and what the graph neural networks are doing. This node will receive a message from all the other nodes that are neighbors with this node.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.02082984335720539, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>Databases'}, {'relevance': 0.008074851706624031, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>DataStorageAndWarehousing'}, {'relevance': 0.007804304361343384, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>3-DGraphics'}, {'relevance': 0.0026231221854686737, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ProgrammingLanguages'}, {'relevance': 0.002109952736645937, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.0009530577226541936, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerNetworking'}, {'relevance': 0.0003064601041842252, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.00026426606927998364, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Robotics'}, {'relevance': 0.0002067683672066778, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>EndocrineAndMetabolicDiseases>HormonalDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.00019636192882899195, 'label': 'Sports>InlineSkating'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 1025968, 'end': 1061600}, 'sentences_idx_start': 151, 'sentences_idx_end': 154}, {'text': "And this message can also be passed, can use some neural networks in there, but essentially it's some processing of these features of the neighbors and these are aggregated into this message. So here in Green and then this is passed through some update function that combines the message from the neighbors with the old representation of this node and it gives you a new representation at the next layer. And this happens for all the nodes, right?", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.08590634912252426, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerNetworking'}, {'relevance': 0.01000512670725584, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>InternetOfThings'}, {'relevance': 0.004490068182349205, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>Databases'}, {'relevance': 0.0031006354838609695, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>OperatingSystems'}, {'relevance': 0.0020244293846189976, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.00197825045324862, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>DataStorageAndWarehousing'}, {'relevance': 0.0011651780223473907, 'label': 'Home&Garden>SmartHome'}, {'relevance': 0.0010443630162626505, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Robotics'}, {'relevance': 0.0007624588324688375, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>CloudComputing'}, {'relevance': 0.0005763106746599078, 'label': 'Science>SpaceAndAstronomy'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 1061940, 'end': 1090296}, 'sentences_idx_start': 155, 'sentences_idx_end': 157}, {'text': "So then you get some new representations for this node and this is one layer and then you kind of keep repeating this for as many layers as you like. So this is kind of how you do deep learning on graphs. It's kind of a very simple recipe and most models actually vary in the way they kind of compute these messages and in the way this update function is designed. But that's kind of the parameters most of these models use.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.04782507196068764, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>Databases'}, {'relevance': 0.01755291409790516, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>DataStorageAndWarehousing'}, {'relevance': 0.012875172309577465, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>3-DGraphics'}, {'relevance': 0.00431691762059927, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ProgrammingLanguages'}, {'relevance': 0.002307937713339925, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.0011536969104781747, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.00035840453347191215, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Robotics'}, {'relevance': 0.00027012632926926017, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>GenealogyAndAncestry'}, {'relevance': 0.0002695719012990594, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>CloudComputing'}, {'relevance': 0.00024392329214606434, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>EndocrineAndMetabolicDiseases>HormonalDisorders'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 1090318, 'end': 1116176}, 'sentences_idx_start': 158, 'sentences_idx_end': 161}, {'text': "Otherwise they all kind of respect this framework and work in this kind of particular way. And to give you maybe an example for why you would want to do this, you might want to do node classification. This is kind of a classic problem in graph machine learning. There are others, but I'm just going to talk about this because it's easier. So you have a graph and this graph has nodes that have different labels. Here there's just two kinds of labels, this orange and blue.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.01677519828081131, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>Databases'}, {'relevance': 0.010122071020305157, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ProgrammingLanguages'}, {'relevance': 0.004911062773317099, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.0037910270038992167, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>DataStorageAndWarehousing'}, {'relevance': 0.002087055239826441, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>3-DGraphics'}, {'relevance': 0.0018264853861182928, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.0004807380901183933, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Robotics'}, {'relevance': 0.0004351493262220174, 'label': 'Science>Genetics'}, {'relevance': 0.0003624922246672213, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>GenealogyAndAncestry'}, {'relevance': 0.0003387261531315744, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>Search'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 1116358, 'end': 1145980}, 'sentences_idx_start': 162, 'sentences_idx_end': 167}, {'text': "And you have some edges between these nodes. And what you want is you want to do this kind of message passing that I was describing to compute some representations for these nodes where you can easily classify the blue and orange nodes. Now something that's quite interesting is that for many kind of graph neural networks, depending on the properties of these graphs and how these kind of different nodes are connected, their performance might vary quite a lot. So in particular they're affected by this property called heterophili.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.004011714365333319, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ProgrammingLanguages'}, {'relevance': 0.0031800337601453066, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.0027076592668890953, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>3-DGraphics'}, {'relevance': 0.002378785517066717, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.0021976535208523273, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>Databases'}, {'relevance': 0.0014664067421108484, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Robotics'}, {'relevance': 0.0007473657024092972, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>DataStorageAndWarehousing'}, {'relevance': 0.00021955589181743562, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>EndocrineAndMetabolicDiseases>HormonalDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.00021732423920184374, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>VirtualReality'}, {'relevance': 0.00021134421695023775, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerNetworking'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 1147600, 'end': 1183876}, 'sentences_idx_start': 168, 'sentences_idx_end': 171}, {'text': 'So this is kind of a measure of how much opposites attractive you want, right? So it has a very simple formula. Basically you take the number of edges between orange and blue nodes and you divide by the total number of edges, right? So basically you kind of check how many connections we have in this graph between things that are quite opposite to each other versus connections that are between similar kind of nodes.', 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.11021842807531357, 'label': 'Style&Fashion>Beauty'}, {'relevance': 0.0013257772661745548, 'label': 'FamilyAndRelationships>Dating'}, {'relevance': 0.0007825117208994925, 'label': 'Style&Fashion>Beauty>PerfumeAndFragrance'}, {'relevance': 0.000631527160294354, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Astrology'}, {'relevance': 0.0004959744983352721, 'label': 'Science>SpaceAndAstronomy'}, {'relevance': 0.0003094190906267613, 'label': "HealthyLiving>Men'sHealth"}, {'relevance': 0.0002804354589898139, 'label': 'BooksAndLiterature>Poetry'}, {'relevance': 0.00026093097403645515, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>ReproductiveHealth>BirthControl'}, {'relevance': 0.00023093787604011595, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>3-DGraphics'}, {'relevance': 0.00022240509861148894, 'label': 'Science>Chemistry'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 1184068, 'end': 1209836}, 'sentences_idx_start': 172, 'sentences_idx_end': 175}, {'text': "So if you have a lot of these kind of heterogeneous connections, then you have very high heterophili. And it turns out that many graphene networks actually struggle in that setting. It's very hard to classify things in that setting. And intuitively you could kind of also figure out why because you could easily apply some kind of reasoning where oh, this node looks a lot like this other node is connected to. So they kind of must be in the same community if you want or in the same label.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.19915461540222168, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerNetworking'}, {'relevance': 0.001723609515465796, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>InternetOfThings'}, {'relevance': 0.0007157595246098936, 'label': 'Science>Chemistry'}, {'relevance': 0.0005181377055123448, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet'}, {'relevance': 0.0004826615331694484, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerPeripherals'}, {'relevance': 0.00033055993844754994, 'label': 'Science>SpaceAndAstronomy'}, {'relevance': 0.0002681234327610582, 'label': 'Home&Garden>SmartHome'}, {'relevance': 0.0002392046881141141, 'label': 'Science>Physics'}, {'relevance': 0.00021543589537031949, 'label': 'PersonalFinance>HomeUtilities>InternetServiceProviders'}, {'relevance': 0.00020681411842815578, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>ITAndInternetSupport'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 1210028, 'end': 1241480}, 'sentences_idx_start': 176, 'sentences_idx_end': 180}, {'text': "But it's much harder to do that when all things are kind of different from each other and these communities kind of don't form right, even visually. If you see a graph and it has some nicely clustered communities, it's quite easy to draw a line between those and say, oh, this is a community, is another community. But if things are very mixed, then it's quite challenging.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.27627214789390564, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>SocialNetworking'}, {'relevance': 0.08881029486656189, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ContentProduction'}, {'relevance': 0.009501402266323566, 'label': 'VideoGaming>VideoGameGenres>MMOs'}, {'relevance': 0.0016986948903650045, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>InternetForBeginners'}, {'relevance': 0.0009696969646029174, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet'}, {'relevance': 0.0008537271060049534, 'label': 'FamilyAndRelationships>Parenting>InternetSafety'}, {'relevance': 0.0007612337358295918, 'label': 'Science>Geography'}, {'relevance': 0.0006172121502459049, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>DataStorageAndWarehousing'}, {'relevance': 0.00048248490202240646, 'label': 'Home&Garden>IndoorEnvironmentalQuality'}, {'relevance': 0.00047321466263383627, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>GamesAndPuzzles>RoleplayingGames'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 1241560, 'end': 1263692}, 'sentences_idx_start': 181, 'sentences_idx_end': 183}, {'text': "And it turns out it's also challenging for these models, not just for kind of our intuition when we would have to do this. So this is kind of some problem where this topological perspective I was mentioning will be used to do some useful stuff. Okay? So coming back to Sheaves on graphs. And at this point I think you can largely forget what I mentioned in the introduction or if there's something you misunderstood there. We kind of start from zero bit here, so there's no problem.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.018227433785796165, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>3-DGraphics'}, {'relevance': 0.002975258743390441, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>Databases'}, {'relevance': 0.0010790989035740495, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>DataStorageAndWarehousing'}, {'relevance': 0.0007489299168810248, 'label': 'Science>Physics'}, {'relevance': 0.0007154789054766297, 'label': 'VideoGaming>VideoGameGenres>SimulationVideoGames'}, {'relevance': 0.0005119411507621408, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ProgrammingLanguages'}, {'relevance': 0.0004634121141862124, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>VirtualReality'}, {'relevance': 0.0003343719581607729, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>GraphicsSoftware'}, {'relevance': 0.00028861715691164136, 'label': 'Science>Geography'}, {'relevance': 0.00025362794985994697, 'label': 'VideoGaming>VideoGameGenres>PuzzleVideoGames'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 1263756, 'end': 1300300}, 'sentences_idx_start': 184, 'sentences_idx_end': 189}, {'text': "So on the left you just have a graph which is kind of the incidence structure of a graph. I just drawn here the simplest possible graph that has two nodes v and U. And then there's an edge between them. So this is just a graph with one edge. That's all that's going on here. And I've just represented it by kind of in this kind of incidence structure kind of way, right?", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.15108667314052582, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>3-DGraphics'}, {'relevance': 0.004634902346879244, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ArtsAndCrafts>DrawingAndSketching'}, {'relevance': 0.0033126636408269405, 'label': 'Science>Geography'}, {'relevance': 0.0010506520047783852, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>GraphicsSoftware'}, {'relevance': 0.0006625234382227063, 'label': 'FineArt>Design'}, {'relevance': 0.0005418176879175007, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>ComputerAnimation'}, {'relevance': 0.0005129636847414076, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>PhotoEditingSoftware'}, {'relevance': 0.00044279592111706734, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>DataStorageAndWarehousing'}, {'relevance': 0.0004097225028090179, 'label': 'VideoGaming>VideoGameGenres>PuzzleVideoGames'}, {'relevance': 0.00036238651955500245, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>Databases'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 1300370, 'end': 1323236}, 'sentences_idx_start': 190, 'sentences_idx_end': 195}, {'text': "Node v is incident to node e and node u, sorry, edge e and node U is incident to edge e. So this is just an incident structure and what this kind of triangle symbol is showing is just this incident structure. It's just a way to symbolize this incidence relation if you want. Okay, so this is just a graph, right? And a way we can kind of think of field zone graphs is just mapping this graph structure. So this is kind of this categorical theory translation.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.017050670459866524, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>Databases'}, {'relevance': 0.008581386879086494, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>DataStorageAndWarehousing'}, {'relevance': 0.007650940679013729, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerNetworking'}, {'relevance': 0.0004863455833401531, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>3-DGraphics'}, {'relevance': 0.00041174443322233856, 'label': 'Science>Geography'}, {'relevance': 0.00024215316807385534, 'label': 'Science>SpaceAndAstronomy'}, {'relevance': 0.00017223473696503788, 'label': 'VideoGaming>VideoGameGenres>SimulationVideoGames'}, {'relevance': 0.0001630529441172257, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>MedicalTests'}, {'relevance': 0.00015613801951985806, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>OperatingSystems'}, {'relevance': 0.00014827823906671256, 'label': 'Science>Chemistry'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 1323338, 'end': 1351528}, 'sentences_idx_start': 196, 'sentences_idx_end': 201}, {'text': "We translate this graph into something else which looks very similar. The structure is kind of the same, it's just kind of the meaning of these things change. So for each node v we have here, this will be a vector space. So F of v is a vector space. For each node u we have F of U which is another vector space. For each edge e we have this Fe which is another vector space.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.019788753241300583, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>Databases'}, {'relevance': 0.0035760116297751665, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>3-DGraphics'}, {'relevance': 0.0026874933391809464, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>DataStorageAndWarehousing'}, {'relevance': 0.0007364362827502191, 'label': 'Science>Geography'}, {'relevance': 0.0004981387755833566, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerNetworking'}, {'relevance': 0.00033751685987226665, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ProgrammingLanguages'}, {'relevance': 0.00026034796610474586, 'label': 'VideoGaming>VideoGameGenres>PuzzleVideoGames'}, {'relevance': 0.00023342343047261238, 'label': 'FamilyAndRelationships'}, {'relevance': 0.0001666634198045358, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>GenealogyAndAncestry'}, {'relevance': 0.0001460843050153926, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>GamesAndPuzzles'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 1351624, 'end': 1377190}, 'sentences_idx_start': 202, 'sentences_idx_end': 207}, {'text': "So all nodes have their own vector spaces and the features associated to those nodes leaving those vector spaces. So basically for each node we have a vector space of features that's all that's going on so far. And also these arrows that these incidence relations also translate into something and they translate into the obvious thing linear maps. So if these are vector spaces, then these things should be linear maps or just some matrices essentially, right?", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.024034323170781136, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerNetworking'}, {'relevance': 0.005264075007289648, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>Databases'}, {'relevance': 0.0020258971489965916, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>DataStorageAndWarehousing'}, {'relevance': 0.0005785312969237566, 'label': 'Science>SpaceAndAstronomy'}, {'relevance': 0.0003971180703956634, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerPeripherals'}, {'relevance': 0.00038191615021787584, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>OperatingSystems'}, {'relevance': 0.0003035991103388369, 'label': 'Home&Garden>IndoorEnvironmentalQuality'}, {'relevance': 0.00022526421525981277, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>3-DGraphics'}, {'relevance': 0.00019863407942466438, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>InternetOfThings'}, {'relevance': 0.00015273920143954456, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>InformationAndNetworkSecurity'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 1377640, 'end': 1404272}, 'sentences_idx_start': 208, 'sentences_idx_end': 211}, {'text': "So for each arrow you see here we have a matrix and something that I'll argue and show in a few slides is that basically message passing is very similar on graphs, is very similar with group actions in group theory. So let me explain exactly why. So we kind of can think of what we have on the left these arrows from the incidence relation. We could think of these arrows as kind of some buttons we can press. So what do I mean by that?", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.017394058406352997, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>SocialNetworking'}, {'relevance': 0.012171855196356773, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>Email'}, {'relevance': 0.0026574134826660156, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerNetworking'}, {'relevance': 0.0023325136862695217, 'label': 'FamilyAndRelationships>Dating'}, {'relevance': 0.0015616480959579349, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ProgrammingLanguages'}, {'relevance': 0.0009942860342562199, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>Databases'}, {'relevance': 0.0009485187474638224, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>WebConferencing'}, {'relevance': 0.000663305283524096, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>DataStorageAndWarehousing'}, {'relevance': 0.0005581947043538094, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>InternetForBeginners'}, {'relevance': 0.0004776058776769787, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ContentProduction'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 1404326, 'end': 1442476}, 'sentences_idx_start': 212, 'sentences_idx_end': 216}, {'text': "So if we have this node v on the left, right, and this e, now if we have some features, some feature living in FOV, right, we could just kind of press this arrow button here and then if we multiply this matrix by this feature, we will get an edge feature. So it's kind of like if you go along this arrow, this matrix will multiply this feature and this vertex feature and it will give you an edge feature.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.0843549594283104, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>3-DGraphics'}, {'relevance': 0.0017471503233537078, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>Databases'}, {'relevance': 0.0009697080822661519, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ProgrammingLanguages'}, {'relevance': 0.0008552232175134122, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>DataStorageAndWarehousing'}, {'relevance': 0.0007662365678697824, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>AugmentedReality'}, {'relevance': 0.0003491683746688068, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>PhotoEditingSoftware'}, {'relevance': 0.0003257692151237279, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerNetworking'}, {'relevance': 0.00028743635630235076, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>GraphicsSoftware'}, {'relevance': 0.0002678610326256603, 'label': 'Science>SpaceAndAstronomy'}, {'relevance': 0.0002571436925791204, 'label': 'Sports>InlineSkating'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 1442578, 'end': 1472816}, 'sentences_idx_start': 217, 'sentences_idx_end': 218}, {'text': "So you could think of these arrows as kind of giving you some sort of actions that you can play with to move features from vertex to edge and edge to vertex. So in this case it's kind of a left action, right? So this is what I'm saying. I'm taking this arrow, which is this one here, and I act on some features of node v.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.014949915930628777, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>3-DGraphics'}, {'relevance': 0.002739720745012164, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ProgrammingLanguages'}, {'relevance': 0.0005227579968050122, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>AugmentedReality'}, {'relevance': 0.0003614557790569961, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Robotics'}, {'relevance': 0.00026057346258312464, 'label': 'VideoGaming>VideoGameGenres>PuzzleVideoGames'}, {'relevance': 0.00019213058112654835, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerNetworking'}, {'relevance': 0.0001851828274084255, 'label': 'Sports>FieldHockey'}, {'relevance': 0.0001814853894757107, 'label': 'Science>Genetics'}, {'relevance': 0.0001709065109025687, 'label': 'VideoGaming>VideoGameGenres>SimulationVideoGames'}, {'relevance': 0.00015787387383170426, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>VirtualReality'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 1473008, 'end': 1490872}, 'sentences_idx_start': 219, 'sentences_idx_end': 222}, {'text': "So this HOV that lives here and how I do that is I just take this matrix, this matrix associated with this arrow, and I multiply this vector HOV. So just matrix times vector, that's all. And then we get an edge feature. So this is just kind of a way to move from here to here. So this already kind of looks a bit like message passing, right?", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.02088339626789093, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>3-DGraphics'}, {'relevance': 0.016142025589942932, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ProgrammingLanguages'}, {'relevance': 0.0011722680646926165, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>AugmentedReality'}, {'relevance': 0.0006353798671625555, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>OperatingSystems'}, {'relevance': 0.0006021165172569454, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerPeripherals'}, {'relevance': 0.0005994358798488975, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Robotics'}, {'relevance': 0.0005172680248506367, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>WebDevelopment'}, {'relevance': 0.0005101895658299327, 'label': 'VideoGaming>VideoGameGenres>PuzzleVideoGames'}, {'relevance': 0.0004177657247055322, 'label': 'VideoGaming>VideoGameGenres>SimulationVideoGames'}, {'relevance': 0.0003388114273548126, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>WebDesignAndHTML'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 1490926, 'end': 1513616}, 'sentences_idx_start': 223, 'sentences_idx_end': 227}, {'text': "We're kind of passing a message from this vertex to this edge, but now we also need to pass a message from this edge to these other vertex U. So we need to get from V to U and we did that by passing through e. So by doing that, we could do that by kind of going in reverse. So we could have a right action where instead of applying this matrix, we applied adjoint matrix. So that's just a transpose matrix.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.024879904463887215, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>3-DGraphics'}, {'relevance': 0.0033347811549901962, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>Databases'}, {'relevance': 0.002089018700644374, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ProgrammingLanguages'}, {'relevance': 0.001809866400435567, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>DataStorageAndWarehousing'}, {'relevance': 0.0006666029221378267, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerNetworking'}, {'relevance': 0.0004571067402139306, 'label': 'Science>Physics'}, {'relevance': 0.0003275046474300325, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerPeripherals'}, {'relevance': 0.00028184265829622746, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>OperatingSystems'}, {'relevance': 0.00024952119565568864, 'label': 'VideoGaming>VideoGameGenres>PuzzleVideoGames'}, {'relevance': 0.00017630061483941972, 'label': 'Sports>InlineSkating'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 1513638, 'end': 1543016}, 'sentences_idx_start': 228, 'sentences_idx_end': 232}, {'text': "So if we want to go from here to here, instead of applying this matrix, we apply it transpose because we want to go the other way around. If we compose these things, then we can move features from V to U. So this is just a way that kind of we can apply these actions to do message passing and these are called shift actions or preshift actions. And I'm going to now show what's kind of the relation between this and what we have in group theory.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.2970781624317169, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ProgrammingLanguages'}, {'relevance': 0.015748104080557823, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>Databases'}, {'relevance': 0.00975106656551361, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>OperatingSystems'}, {'relevance': 0.004834465682506561, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>DataStorageAndWarehousing'}, {'relevance': 0.003157869214192033, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerNetworking'}, {'relevance': 0.0024630294647067785, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.001686655916273594, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerPeripherals'}, {'relevance': 0.0010293973609805107, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>3-DGraphics'}, {'relevance': 0.0007849651738069952, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>DigitalAudio'}, {'relevance': 0.0005191729869693518, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 1543128, 'end': 1576260}, 'sentences_idx_start': 233, 'sentences_idx_end': 236}, {'text': "So one way to represent a group is by kind of having some sort of graph, like here on the left. So we kind of have some star object, it's just kind of a dummy thing there. But all the group structure is in these arrows, right? So for each group element. So let's say this g is a 90 degree rotation, for instance. Let's say we do have a group of rotations, just to have some concrete example.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.011587909422814846, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>Databases'}, {'relevance': 0.002614608034491539, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ProgrammingLanguages'}, {'relevance': 0.0018281700322404504, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>DataStorageAndWarehousing'}, {'relevance': 0.0011660957243293524, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>3-DGraphics'}, {'relevance': 0.0011289092944934964, 'label': 'Science>Chemistry'}, {'relevance': 0.00033976740087382495, 'label': 'Science>Genetics'}, {'relevance': 0.0002793997118715197, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerNetworking'}, {'relevance': 0.00020711722027044743, 'label': 'Science>Physics'}, {'relevance': 0.00018197490135207772, 'label': 'Science>BiologicalSciences'}, {'relevance': 0.0001755116245476529, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 1577100, 'end': 1606530}, 'sentences_idx_start': 237, 'sentences_idx_end': 242}, {'text': "So this arrow could correspond to a 90 degree rotation. We have another arrow that does the opposite, minus kind of 90 degree rotation. That's the inverse of that transformation. So this is kind of the structure of this group. And if we have, we also do this similar kind of translation as we've just seen. So basically we define a preshift on this group. We map this star to a vector space. So the star kind of replaces the vertex we had before.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.9555744528770447, 'label': 'Science>SpaceAndAstronomy'}, {'relevance': 0.005721006542444229, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Astrology'}, {'relevance': 0.0015337353106588125, 'label': 'Science>Physics'}, {'relevance': 0.0009186481474898756, 'label': 'Science>Geography'}, {'relevance': 0.0007341347518377006, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>3-DGraphics'}, {'relevance': 0.0004832970444113016, 'label': 'NewsAndPolitics>Weather'}, {'relevance': 0.00021712126908823848, 'label': 'Pets>Birds'}, {'relevance': 0.00020048583974130452, 'label': 'Science>Geology'}, {'relevance': 0.00015368119056802243, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAn