u apply this rotation matrix on v and you get like a 90 degree rotation here. So this is what's going on.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.03775826841592789, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>3-DGraphics'}, {'relevance': 0.004960227757692337, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ProgrammingLanguages'}, {'relevance': 0.0035137247759848833, 'label': 'Science>Physics'}, {'relevance': 0.0005963555304333568, 'label': 'VideoGaming>VideoGameGenres>SimulationVideoGames'}, {'relevance': 0.0004887020913884044, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.00040656086639501154, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>Databases'}, {'relevance': 0.0003505821223370731, 'label': 'VideoGaming>VideoGameGenres>PuzzleVideoGames'}, {'relevance': 0.0002872068143915385, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>DigitalAudio'}, {'relevance': 0.0002658604644238949, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>DataStorageAndWarehousing'}, {'relevance': 0.00023508560843765736, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>GraphicsSoftware'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 1658758, 'end': 1688792}, 'sentences_idx_start': 255, 'sentences_idx_end': 259}, {'text': "This kind of vertical vector is showing the rotated vector. So this is completely analogous with what we've seen on the previous slide. This is how kind of sheaves connect these kind of actions. So essentially what you could think of as message passing is same as group actions in group theory, but you just replace this group with a graph. So it's kind of analogous to that, right? So it's just kind of a different kind of translations where we replace the object on the left.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.49470722675323486, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ProgrammingLanguages'}, {'relevance': 0.022709950804710388, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>Databases'}, {'relevance': 0.006137923337519169, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>DataStorageAndWarehousing'}, {'relevance': 0.005085107870399952, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerNetworking'}, {'relevance': 0.004753426648676395, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>OperatingSystems'}, {'relevance': 0.003499432234093547, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.0018651621649041772, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>3-DGraphics'}, {'relevance': 0.0015261656371876597, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerPeripherals'}, {'relevance': 0.0011230518575757742, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications'}, {'relevance': 0.0006689148722216487, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>WebDevelopment'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 1688846, 'end': 1719270}, 'sentences_idx_start': 260, 'sentences_idx_end': 265}, {'text': 'Now it looks like this is a graph, this is a group, right? But kind of the rest stays exactly the same. And this kind of gives us a way to formalize in a way by looking in this topological perspective to connect all these kind of symmetries and things like that that have been explored quite a lot in machine learning to message passing on graphs and to see one way in which they are related.', 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.07483910024166107, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ProgrammingLanguages'}, {'relevance': 0.0222354456782341, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>Databases'}, {'relevance': 0.01210679393261671, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.008935374207794666, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.0056693060323596, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>DataStorageAndWarehousing'}, {'relevance': 0.005609313026070595, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>3-DGraphics'}, {'relevance': 0.001446735579520464, 'label': 'Science>Physics'}, {'relevance': 0.0007435469888150692, 'label': 'Science'}, {'relevance': 0.000574688718188554, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Robotics'}, {'relevance': 0.0004054848977830261, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>GamesAndPuzzles'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 1719720, 'end': 1741740}, 'sentences_idx_start': 266, 'sentences_idx_end': 268}, {'text': "Okay, so now you might say, okay, this was all very sophisticated and nice, but you know, what, is this going anywhere, basically? And I'm just going to show you kind of a very short example. There's more, but the time is limited. And something we showed is that, as I was saying in the beginning, many graph neural networks kind of struggle in these heterophilic graphs.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.11786650121212006, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.03205148130655289, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ProgrammingLanguages'}, {'relevance': 0.01319208461791277, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>3-DGraphics'}, {'relevance': 0.010951868258416653, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.0015023048035800457, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>Databases'}, {'relevance': 0.0008261214243248105, 'label': 'VideoGaming>VideoGameGenres>SimulationVideoGames'}, {'relevance': 0.0007294376264326274, 'label': 'Technology&Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.0006806402816437185, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Robotics'}, {'relevance': 0.0006776513182558119, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>GraphicsSoftware'}, {'relevance': 0.0005079923430457711, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>DataStorageAndWarehousing'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 1742720, 'end': 1766508}, 'sentences_idx_start': 269, 'sentences_idx_end': 272}, {'text': "And what we showed is that no matter how heterophilic or kind of weird your graph is, you can always kind of find some shift structure, essentially kind of a message passing neural network, that if you use sufficient layers, it will be able to disentangle the classes of the nodes, right? So just to show you in this picture what you have here on the very far left, the colors of the nodes, they show the class. So there's three colors here. So three classes, right?", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.01539972610771656, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>Databases'}, {'relevance': 0.002107546664774418, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>3-DGraphics'}, {'relevance': 0.0016647420125082135, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ProgrammingLanguages'}, {'relevance': 0.0011281181359663606, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>DataStorageAndWarehousing'}, {'relevance': 0.0007465335656888783, 'label': 'Science>Genetics'}, {'relevance': 0.0004643502470571548, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerNetworking'}, {'relevance': 0.00035146225127391517, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>GenealogyAndAncestry'}, {'relevance': 0.0003342432319186628, 'label': 'Science>Geography'}, {'relevance': 0.00032517904764972627, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.00016988583956845105, 'label': 'Education>EducationalAssessment>StandardizedTesting'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 1766604, 'end': 1801150}, 'sentences_idx_start': 273, 'sentences_idx_end': 276}, {'text': "And this is kind of the graph in the beginning and the position of the nodes in this box denotes the features. So that's a way to kind of just to visualize the features. The 2D position is actually the 2D feature vector of each node. And you can see in the beginning, everything is kind of super messy and entangled, right? Like if you want to classify these nodes, it's kind of very hard because their representations, their initial representations are very messy and kind of intertwined.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.04631390422582626, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>3-DGraphics'}, {'relevance': 0.0037980210036039352, 'label': 'Science>Geography'}, {'relevance': 0.001678678672760725, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>Databases'}, {'relevance': 0.0010919413762167096, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>DataStorageAndWarehousing'}, {'relevance': 0.0003550297114998102, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Industries>LogisticsAndTransportationIndustry'}, {'relevance': 0.0003250020672567189, 'label': 'Home&Garden>Landscaping'}, {'relevance': 0.0003051888488698751, 'label': 'Science>SpaceAndAstronomy'}, {'relevance': 0.0002287595416419208, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerNetworking'}, {'relevance': 0.00022513882140628994, 'label': 'Science>Geology'}, {'relevance': 0.0002185589837608859, 'label': 'VideoGaming>VideoGameGenres>PuzzleVideoGames'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 1801520, 'end': 1830280}, 'sentences_idx_start': 277, 'sentences_idx_end': 281}, {'text': "But as we stack more layers of a particular kind of sheath or a message passing model, you see how progressively these classes get kind of more disentangled and more disentangled at each new layer. So these representations kind of collapse and they form these kind of clusterings, right? And then when you get with something like at the end, you can kind of see these three communities very clearly and it's extremely easy to separate.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.2948763370513916, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerNetworking'}, {'relevance': 0.2742437422275543, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>Databases'}, {'relevance': 0.06625165790319443, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>DataStorageAndWarehousing'}, {'relevance': 0.050487883388996124, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ProgrammingLanguages'}, {'relevance': 0.01114905346184969, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>OperatingSystems'}, {'relevance': 0.0023808730766177177, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications'}, {'relevance': 0.0020766647066920996, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.0019453410059213638, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>Email'}, {'relevance': 0.001621532835997641, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>WebDevelopment'}, {'relevance': 0.001334093976765871, 'label': 'PersonalFinance>HomeUtilities>PhoneServices'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 1830780, 'end': 1858640}, 'sentences_idx_start': 282, 'sentences_idx_end': 284}, {'text': 'And kind of the essence behind these results was we showed for different kinds of problems what sorts of chief or message passing models you need by using this theory to solve kind of problems. And this is quite important because it kind of shows you some important bits and pieces in the architecture that you might want to kind of change or use in order to solve certain kinds of problems. And we also had some sort of impossibility resolved.', 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.2378518283367157, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerNetworking'}, {'relevance': 0.129746675491333, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ProgrammingLanguages'}, {'relevance': 0.05962001904845238, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>OperatingSystems'}, {'relevance': 0.008207899518311024, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>Email'}, {'relevance': 0.006664746440947056, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.006276706699281931, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>Databases'}, {'relevance': 0.005603599827736616, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>WebDevelopment'}, {'relevance': 0.005477705504745245, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>ITAndInternetSupport'}, {'relevance': 0.004973160568624735, 'label': 'PersonalFinance>HomeUtilities>PhoneServices'}, {'relevance': 0.004420192912220955, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>DataStorageAndWarehousing'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 1859140, 'end': 1888196}, 'sentences_idx_start': 285, 'sentences_idx_end': 287}, {'text': "So if you use a graph neural network of some kind, you can't solve this problem or you'll struggle to solve this problem. And we also saw, okay, if you use some more general ones, then you might have a chance. So this is kind of some high level view behind this theoretical stuff. And what we actually do in practice is to essentially learn these message passing functions or to learn the sheath or these matrices.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.6804141998291016, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.07384345680475235, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ProgrammingLanguages'}, {'relevance': 0.04070672020316124, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.00476309796795249, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>Databases'}, {'relevance': 0.0024238694459199905, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>3-DGraphics'}, {'relevance': 0.0020062336698174477, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Robotics'}, {'relevance': 0.0015159862814471126, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>DataStorageAndWarehousing'}, {'relevance': 0.0015145953511819243, 'label': 'Technology&Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.0014308015815913677, 'label': 'VideoGaming>VideoGameGenres>SimulationVideoGames'}, {'relevance': 0.0009720571688376367, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>GamesAndPuzzles'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 1888228, 'end': 1919072}, 'sentences_idx_start': 288, 'sentences_idx_end': 291}, {'text': "So in practice, like when someone gives you a node classification task, it's very hard to know beforehand what exactly is the right sheep or the right message passing model to solve that task. And what we do essentially, we learn that from data. So we learn these matrices that do the message passing. We learn them from data by using some neural networks which are shown here in red. And then you learn how to kind of transfer features between these vector spaces and kind of move them around.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.5444213151931763, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.07563561201095581, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.031018024310469627, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ProgrammingLanguages'}, {'relevance': 0.0035913223400712013, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>Databases'}, {'relevance': 0.0032206883188337088, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Robotics'}, {'relevance': 0.0024901810102164745, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>DataStorageAndWarehousing'}, {'relevance': 0.0016035494627431035, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>InternetOfThings'}, {'relevance': 0.0015143003547564149, 'label': 'Technology&Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.001071902341209352, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>Beekeeping'}, {'relevance': 0.0007954032043926418, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>3-DGraphics'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 1919216, 'end': 1955116}, 'sentences_idx_start': 292, 'sentences_idx_end': 296}, {'text': "So this is just showing how these vectors, which are features of these nodes and edges, how they're kind of moved around by kind of going through via these matrices, just some matrix multiplications. Okay, so that's kind of the high level view behind this model. And we evaluated this on some kind of real world heterophilic data sets where you have to classify nodes based on kind of various communities or different kinds of labels.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.052021902054548264, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>Databases'}, {'relevance': 0.0417122058570385, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>DataStorageAndWarehousing'}, {'relevance': 0.0030301951337605715, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerNetworking'}, {'relevance': 0.001830453984439373, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>3-DGraphics'}, {'relevance': 0.000848983065225184, 'label': 'Science>Genetics'}, {'relevance': 0.0008126832544803619, 'label': 'Science>BiologicalSciences'}, {'relevance': 0.0004990388988517225, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerPeripherals'}, {'relevance': 0.00047000692575238645, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Industries>LogisticsAndTransportationIndustry'}, {'relevance': 0.00033578521106392145, 'label': 'Science>Geography'}, {'relevance': 0.0003249487781431526, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>MedicalTests'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 1955218, 'end': 1983348}, 'sentences_idx_start': 297, 'sentences_idx_end': 299}, {'text': 'And these data sets going from right to left, they are getting more heterophilic. So in some sense more challenging for classic architectures. And our models, which are kind of inspired by all this stuff that I mentioned, they score quite highly in these benchmarks. And at the same time, they also revealed some or justified some various choices that other models in this space have done. But maybe they were not so well justified, or maybe they had different kind of motivations.', 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.09159427881240845, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>DataStorageAndWarehousing'}, {'relevance': 0.06125747784972191, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>Databases'}, {'relevance': 0.0310346819460392, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ProgrammingLanguages'}, {'relevance': 0.002649442059919238, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.0021891614887863398, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.0012534973211586475, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>3-DGraphics'}, {'relevance': 0.001029085018672049, 'label': 'Science'}, {'relevance': 0.0008408937137573957, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Business>BusinessI.T.'}, {'relevance': 0.0007909524720162153, 'label': 'Science>Genetics'}, {'relevance': 0.0007352602551691234, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>OperatingSystems'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 1983444, 'end': 2014252}, 'sentences_idx_start': 300, 'sentences_idx_end': 304}, {'text': "We also managed to kind of show why various things they were already doing, why they made sense from the point of view of this kind of theory. All right, well, that's all I had. Yeah, thanks for listening and yeah, happy to chat more about this and also have lots of backup slides in case, depending on how far we venture off with this question. Cool. Well, awesome work. Thank you for the presentation.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.8634647130966187, 'label': 'Science'}, {'relevance': 0.5232611298561096, 'label': 'Science>Physics'}, {'relevance': 0.10066374391317368, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ParanormalPhenomena'}, {'relevance': 0.008343980647623539, 'label': 'Science>SpaceAndAstronomy'}, {'relevance': 0.006394925992935896, 'label': 'Science>Chemistry'}, {'relevance': 0.0028962877113372087, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.0028459581080824137, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.001664099982008338, 'label': 'Technology&Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.0013513538287952542, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Agnosticism'}, {'relevance': 0.0011855339398607612, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>VirtualReality'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 2014316, 'end': 2048568}, 'sentences_idx_start': 305, 'sentences_idx_end': 310}, {'text': "For people who are in the live chat, they can write some questions, but there's many things I think we could talk about. So I want to start with reading a quote from an abstract of the paper by von der Laur, Kudal and DeVries just to kind of ground this in the active inference context and really justify why the message passing approaches that you are describing are helping in the active inference modeling. It's two papers.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.08404334634542465, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>SocialNetworking'}, {'relevance': 0.021364426240324974, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Business>MarketingAndAdvertising'}, {'relevance': 0.011531664989888668, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ContentProduction'}, {'relevance': 0.00835358165204525, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>Search'}, {'relevance': 0.0060052573680877686, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Business>Sales'}, {'relevance': 0.0053002373315393925, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.0048135677352547646, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>WebConferencing'}, {'relevance': 0.004127908498048782, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>Email'}, {'relevance': 0.001753481337800622, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>InternetForBeginners'}, {'relevance': 0.0016604410484433174, 'label': 'Education>OnlineEducation'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 2048744, 'end': 2077216}, 'sentences_idx_start': 311, 'sentences_idx_end': 313}, {'text': "It's called Realizing Synthetic Active Inference Agents and they wrote, with a full message passing account of synthetic active inference agents, it becomes possible to derive and reuse message updates across models and move closer to industrial applications of synthetic active inference framework. So how does knowing the message passing structure help reuse a model across different settings or facilitate the legibility of the model? Right?", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.06006772071123123, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.02900482714176178, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Robotics'}, {'relevance': 0.007965264841914177, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ProgrammingLanguages'}, {'relevance': 0.007553654722869396, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>DataStorageAndWarehousing'}, {'relevance': 0.006006305571645498, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>CloudComputing'}, {'relevance': 0.004256518557667732, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>InternetOfThings'}, {'relevance': 0.004056914709508419, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>Databases'}, {'relevance': 0.004041025880724192, 'label': 'VideoGaming>VideoGameGenres>SimulationVideoGames'}, {'relevance': 0.0037927546072751284, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.0013671850319951773, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>OperatingSystems'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 2077248, 'end': 2110752}, 'sentences_idx_start': 314, 'sentences_idx_end': 316}, {'text': "So first of all, I'm not super familiar with the kind of active inference literature, so you'll have to help me there a bit to anchor maybe the discussions a bit more into that. But I think if I understand correctly, the kind of question you're getting at is basically how can kind of message passing help us generalize in kind of various kinds of settings or maybe from one graph to another and things like that?", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.006368130911141634, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.0054322658106684685, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>Search'}, {'relevance': 0.004569563083350658, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>DataStorageAndWarehousing'}, {'relevance': 0.003965224139392376, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>Databases'}, {'relevance': 0.003561600111424923, 'label': 'Science'}, {'relevance': 0.0019726718310266733, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ProgrammingLanguages'}, {'relevance': 0.0012393330689519644, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>SocialNetworking'}, {'relevance': 0.0010930487187579274, 'label': 'Relig