 each other, but these kind of patterns might kind of be reemerging in multiple like local patterns might reemerge in multiple graphs and that could help you a way to kind of generalize, right?', 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.030518092215061188, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>3-DGraphics'}, {'relevance': 0.0021057683043181896, 'label': 'Science>Geography'}, {'relevance': 0.0016229447210207582, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>DataStorageAndWarehousing'}, {'relevance': 0.0015224578091874719, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>Databases'}, {'relevance': 0.001193449948914349, 'label': 'VideoGaming>VideoGameGenres>PuzzleVideoGames'}, {'relevance': 0.0011806378606706858, 'label': 'Science>Genetics'}, {'relevance': 0.0005716640152968466, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>PhotoEditingSoftware'}, {'relevance': 0.0004804229538422078, 'label': 'Science>BiologicalSciences'}, {'relevance': 0.0004416539741214365, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ArtsAndCrafts>DrawingAndSketching'}, {'relevance': 0.00042205300997011364, 'label': 'Science>SpaceAndAstronomy'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 2166986, 'end': 2190584}, 'sentences_idx_start': 322, 'sentences_idx_end': 323}, {'text': "Like you could see, for instance, if you have clicks, they're super important in kind of when you do social network modeling and things like that because they kind of show this kind of close group of friends, right? They all talk to each other, so they kind of form a click like everyone's connected to each other, right?", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.9987291693687439, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>SocialNetworking'}, {'relevance': 0.2747393846511841, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ContentProduction'}, {'relevance': 0.0024966674391180277, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Business>MarketingAndAdvertising'}, {'relevance': 0.002155176131054759, 'label': 'FamilyAndRelationships>Dating'}, {'