evance': 0.000181891635293141, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>3-DGraphics'}, {'relevance': 0.00014264714263845235, 'label': 'Science>Chemistry'}, {'relevance': 0.00011343722871970385, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerNetworking'}, {'relevance': 0.00010244276927551255, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>OperatingSystems'}, {'relevance': 9.503861656412482e-05, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 2582940, 'end': 2606224}, 'sentences_idx_start': 375, 'sentences_idx_end': 378}, {'text': "But there's also kind of this possibility where these kind of semantics, they override the structural level where you say, okay, I don't need to communicate with this other agent person or whatever. It depends on what these rates actually mean and in what context you are. And then there's also the case where you could do some sort of selective pruning where this matrix depending on so in kind of linear algebra, the matrix has a kernel.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.006787983700633049, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>Databases'}, {'relevance': 0.005754800979048014, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>DataStorageAndWarehousing'}, {'relevance': 0.0027851001359522343, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerNetworking'}, {'relevance': 0.001755852485075593, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ProgrammingLanguages'}, {'relevance': 0.0015204367227852345, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>OperatingSystems'}, {'relevance': 0.000777337874751538, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Economy>InterestRates'}, {'relevance': 0.0006208908162079751, 'label': 'VideoGaming>VideoGameGenres>SimulationVideoGames'}, {'relevance': 0.0004765994381159544, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>InformationAndNetworkSecurity'}, {'relevance': 0.0003466719062998891, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>InternetOfThings'}, {'relevance': 0.000343600899213925, 'label': 'PersonalFinance>PersonalInvesting'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 2606342, 'end': 2635892}, 'sentences_idx_start': 379, 'sentences_idx_end': 381}, {'text': "So it's all the stuff that that matrix sends to zero. So what vectors are sent to zero, right? But not everything will be sent to zero unless you're the zero matrix. So depending on the features of the neighbors, you could also just send some of the neighbors to zero, right? And that kind of removes those neighbors from the equation. They just kind of get they're not factored in anymore.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.0005032998160459101, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>Databases'}, {'relevance': 0.0002843592956196517, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ProgrammingLanguages'}, {'relevance': 0.00021587077935691923, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>DataStorageAndWarehousing'}, {'relevance': 0.00016823837358970195, 'label': 'VideoGaming>VideoGameGenres>SimulationVideoGames'}, {'relevance': 0.00014119429397396743, 'label': 'Automotive>AutoBodyStyles>Sedan'}, {'relevance': 0.0001244226295966655, 'label': 'Science>Physics'}, {'relevance': 0.00011135006207041442, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>3-DGraphics'}, {'relevance': 0.00010575661144685, 'label': 'Science>Genetics'}, {'relevance': 0.00010363310866523534, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>GamesAndPuzzles'}, {'relevance': 8.276751032099128e-05, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>OperatingSystems'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 2635956, 'end': 2660044}, 'sentences_idx_start': 382, 'sentences_idx_end': 387}, {'text': "So you kind of have this it's a way to get this parsity, I guess, that you were also talking about where certain only maybe a small subset of the inputs or kind of only subset of the features are actually kind of doing some meaningful stuff among the neighbors and everything else will be kind of zeroed out. Yeah, that makes me think of the Lasso regression, which tries to set most variables of having an impact of zero so that a few hopefully important variables really pop out in the analysis.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.008678832091391087, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>Databases'}, {'relevance': 0.0037985132075846195, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>DataStorageAndWarehousing'}, {'relevance': 0.0005006187711842358, 'label': 'PersonalFinance>PersonalInvesting>Options'}, {'relevance': 0.0002155258844140917, 'label': 'Shopping>SalesAndPromotions'}, {'relevance': 0.00021093152463436127, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Economy>Commodities'}, {'relevance': 0.00020109559409320354, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ProgrammingLanguages'}, {'relevance': 0.00017103366553783417, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>3-DGraphics'}, {'relevance': 0.00015745367272756994, 'label': 'RealEstate>RetailProperty'}, {'relevance': 0.00014600492431782186, 'label': 'VideoGaming>VideoGameGenres>SimulationVideoGames'}, {'relevance': 0.00013613520422950387, 'label': 'Education>EducationalAssessment'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 2660172, 'end': 2694520}, 'sentences_idx_start': 388, 'sentences_idx_end': 389}, {'text': "But also there's newer techniques, I guess, of attention modeling and reweighting that isn't just like, okay, set five of them to one and then the rest of them to zero. More nuanced. So I think that sparsity with the expressivity is basically the best of both worlds because you do want to have a situation where there is an edge, but the attention being paid to it is zero.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.008589102886617184, 'label': 'Style&Fashion>Beauty'}, {'relevance': 0.007276935502886772, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ArtsAndCrafts>DrawingAndSketching'}, {'relevance': 0.0027219520416110754, 'label': 'Education>EducationalAssessment'}, {'relevance': 0.0012139752507209778, 'label': 'Education>HomeworkAndStudy'}, {'relevance': 0.0008542585419490933, 'label': 'Shopping>SalesAndPromotions'}, {'relevance': 0.0008241262985393405, 'label': 'BooksAndLiterature>Poetry'}, {'relevance': 0.0006402296712622046, 'label': 'FineArt'}, {'relevance': 0.0004568928270600736, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ContentProduction>FreelanceWriting'}, {'relevance': 0.00036760655348189175, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ContentProduction>Screenwriting'}, {'relevance': 0.0003615576424635947, 'label': 'FineArt>DigitalArts'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 2694600, 'end': 2721156}, 'sentences_idx_start': 390, 'sentences_idx_end': 392}, {'text': "So functionally, that doesn't have an update on the belief state, even though in principle the edge exists. And that's why we can model situations where the agent believes they have impact in the world. But actually, just because the edge in principle exists doesn't mean that it has any given impact. And so that allows the articulation of these models where they factorize and keeps interpretable motifs in terms of just little clusters of motifs.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.04006267711520195, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.004987931810319424, 'label': 'EventsAndAttractions>PoliticalEvent'}, {'relevance': 0.0029314153362065554, 'label': 'NewsAndPolitics>Politics>PoliticalIssues'}, {'relevance': 0.001430302276276052, 'label': 'VideoGaming>VideoGameGenres>SimulationVideoGames'}, {'relevance': 0.0013252899516373873, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Robotics'}, {'relevance': 0.0010104014072567225, 'label': 'NewsAndPolitics>Politics'}, {'relevance': 0.0008013524929992855, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>InternetOfThings'}, {'relevance': 0.000559442094527185, 'label': 'Science'}, {'relevance': 0.0005119803827255964, 'label': 'VideoGaming>VideoGameGenres>MMOs'}, {'relevance': 0.00040524298674426973, 'label': 'PersonalFinance>PersonalInvesting'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 2721338, 'end': 2754460}, 'sentences_idx_start': 393, 'sentences_idx_end': 396}, {'text': "Here in our case describing the action perception and cognition types of systems of interest. But people, I believe, already implicitly do this. They will often add an adjective and refer to x kind of active inference. So like deep active inference with a temporal horizon, sophisticated active inference with this kind of nesting. And those are pointing to a given feature. But of course, those features, as we're hoping, should be composable.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.6636754274368286, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.024671990424394608, 'label': 'Science'}, {'relevance': 0.014280926436185837, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Robotics'}, {'relevance': 0.004823118913918734, 'label': 'Technology&Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.0038611767813563347, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ParanormalPhenomena'}, {'relevance': 0.00339777790941298, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.0020130753982812166, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>InternetOfThings'}, {'relevance': 0.0011532227508723736, 'label': 'Science>Physics'}, {'relevance': 0.0007980330265127122, 'label': 'Science>BiologicalSciences'}, {'relevance': 0.000678092532325536, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>BrainAndNervousSystemDisorders'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 2754620, 'end': 2782600}, 'sentences_idx_start': 397, 'sentences_idx_end': 402}, {'text': "And so this seems to be bringing tools that are even more general than just action perception modeling because they're at a lower level of abstraction than any specific system of interest. But where this work and kind of timeless thinking around cybernetic systems come together through the active inference generative model as a Bayes graph, it gets very exciting. Yeah. And maybe also something worth emphasizing here is that even if this kind of semantic level can get rid of some edges, right, by doing this kind of pruning.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.9951360821723938, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.6293995976448059, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Robotics'}, {'relevance': 0.08350483328104019, 'label': 'Technology&Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.04679540544748306, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>InternetOfThings'}, {'relevance': 0.029566045850515366, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.008097505196928978, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ConsumerElectronics>WearableTechnology'}, {'relevance': 0.004555960185825825, 'label': 'Home&Garden>SmartHome'}, {'relevance': 0.004436468705534935, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>AugmentedReality'}, {'relevance': 0.00300139794126153, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>VirtualReality'}, {'relevance': 0.0024135089479386806, 'label': 'VideoGaming>VideoGameGenres>SimulationVideoGames'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 2783500, 'end': 2824224}, 'sentences_idx_start': 403, 'sentences_idx_end': 406}, {'text': "Something it cannot get rid of is the computation. So something that kind of that structural graphs level forces you to do. It kind of tells you what should you spend compute time on, right? Because even if you're going to decide to prune an edge, you still need to decide that which takes compute time. So you still need to look at all your neighbors if you're a node, right, and decide what to prune.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.025535907596349716, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>Databases'}, {'relevance': 0.002623302862048149, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>DataStorageAndWarehousing'}, {'relevance': 0.001266542705707252, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ProgrammingLanguages'}, {'relevance': 0.0010854763677343726, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.0007579376688227057, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>OperatingSystems'}, {'relevance': 0.0006852418882772326, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>3-DGraphics'}, {'relevance': 0.000639940844848752, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerNetworking'}, {'relevance': 0.0003482647589407861, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>CloudComputing'}, {'relevance': 0.0001557683281134814, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Desktops'}, {'relevance': 0.00014747535169590265, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>VirtualReality'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 2824352, 'end': 2851976}, 'sentences_idx_start': 407, 'sentences_idx_end': 411}, {'text': "Or maybe you don't prune anything or whatever, but you have to look at every edge. And one way to look at this is the graph structure defines you a computational graph or kind of a computational series of computational steps you have to execute. And then the kind of the sheet structure or the message passing model actually specifies what those steps are and in what particular way they look. Exactly. That's one point.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.34356170892715454, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ProgrammingLanguages'}, {'relevance': 0.16578663885593414, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.055146776139736176, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>Databases'}, {'relevance': 0.00971142016351223, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>DataStorageAndWarehousing'}, {'relevance': 0.004972690716385841, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>3-DGraphics'}, {'relevance': 0.0036111101508140564, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications'}, {'relevance': 0.0022052903659641743, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerNetworking'}, {'relevance': 0.0014124041190370917, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>OperatingSystems'}, {'relevance': 0.0008466508006677032, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>GraphicsSoftware'}, {'relevance': 0.00041173913632519543, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Business>BusinessI.T.'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 2852008, 'end': 2880840}, 'sentences_idx_start': 412, 'sentences_idx_end': 416}, {'text': "And you also mentioned attention, and actually I'm glad you did, because this is actually quite related and in certain ways more general than attention. And actually, maybe going back to this slide, it might be a nice way to see this. So here basically what happens in attention. Instead of learning these matrices that we learn here in attention, you learn attention coefficients here. So you just learn a scalar. That's the attention coefficient.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.015117824077606201, 'label': 'Education>HomeworkAndStudy'}, {'relevance': 0.01063197199255228, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>SleepDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.007641902659088373, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>EyeAndVisionConditions'}, {'relevance': 0.002121005207300186, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>BrainAndNervousSystemDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.0015130448155105114, 'label': 'FamilyAndRelationships>Parenting>ParentingBabiesAndToddlers'}, {'relevance': 0.0011341101489961147, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>Injuries'}, {'relevance': 0.0009268152061849833, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>VirtualReality'}, {'relevance': 0.0008921343251131475, 'label': 'FamilyAndRelationships>Parenting>ParentingChildrenAged4-11'}, {'relevance': 0.0007690151687711477, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>SocialNetworking'}, {'relevance': 0.000701102486345917, 'label': 'Education>EducationalAssessment'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 2880910, 'end': 2909804}, 'sentences_idx_start': 417, 'sentences_idx_end': 422}, {'text': "How much attention should I pay to essentially this overall edge, let's say, which will be just a scalar? What we do is kind of a bit more complicated because you just learn, how do I transform these neighbors? So it's kind of a whole matrix rather than a single scalar, but there's also some subtle differences. But in a follow up work we did, we also combined this with attention and went a bit more general and that also worked quite well.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.005567160435020924, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>Databases'}, {'relevance': 0.003342649433761835, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>3-DGraphics'}, {'relevance': 0.0023333735298365355, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>DataStorageAndWarehousing'}, {'relevance': 0.00047714108950458467, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ProgrammingLanguages'}, {'relevance': 0.00039826129795983434, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerNetworking'}, {'relevance': 0.0002039468672592193, 'label': 'Science>Physics'}, {'relevance': 0.00019071785209234804, 'label': 'Sports>InlineSkating'}, {'relevance': 0.00013244197180029005, 'label': 'VideoGaming>VideoGameGenres>SimulationVideoGames'}, {'relevance': 0.0001276871917070821, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>BoneAndJointConditions'}, {'relevance': 0.00012124312343075871, 'label': 'Science>Chemistry'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 2909852, 'end': 2940472}, 'sentences_idx_start': 423, 'sentences_idx_end': 426}, {'text': 'But the kind of underlying idea is very similar. You want to modulate the way you transform information based on the information itself, right? So you have this kind of one level of recursivity. If you want that, you are also alluding to that.', 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.5865941047668457, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>DataStorageAndWarehousing'}, {'relevance': 0.12152544409036636, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>Databases'}, {'relevance': 0.04400377348065376, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.042548805475234985, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Business>BusinessI.T.'}, {'relevance': 0.010343687608838081, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ProgrammingLanguages'}, {'relevance': 0.007118068635463715, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Industries>InformationServicesIndustry'}, {'relevance': 0.0052250949665904045, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications'}, {'relevance': 0.001872335560619831, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>3-DGraphics'}, {'relevance': 0.0018146198708564043, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.001443303655833006, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>InformationAndNetworkSecurity'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 2940526, 'end': 2957584}, 'sentences_idx_start': 427, 'sentences_idx_end': 430}, {'text': "It happens in active inference, where, okay, so if I'm node v, right, my neighbor knew it has some features, and based on these features, which are xu, I'm going to find out the matrix that will be used to process xu, right. So it's kind of very recursive and it's what happens with attention, right.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.06600547581911087, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>Databases'}, {'relevance': 0.009094270877540112, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>DataStorageAndWarehousing'}, {'relevance': 0.0029258858412504196, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>Search'}, {'relevance': 0.00032029583235271275, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>InternetOfThings'}, {'relevance': 0.00031550758285447955, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>GenealogyAndAncestry'}, {'relevance': 0.00025111113791354, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>WebDevelopment'}, {'relevance': 0.00021350386668927968, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ProgrammingLanguages'}, {'relevance': 0.00020070848404429853, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>CloudComputing'}, {'relevance': 0.00016929092817008495, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>EndocrineAndMetabolicDiseases>HormonalDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.00016475896700285375, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerNetworking'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 2957702, 'end': 2977348}, 'sentences_idx_start': 431, 'sentences_idx_end': 432}, {'text': "Based on the features of node u, I'm going to compute an attention coefficient that I'm going to apply to this feature of you, right? I'm going to decide based on this feature, how much attention should I pay to it. And here we decide how should I process it more generally in a linear way. So you have this kind of loopiness structure embedded in there. Awesome. I'll bring up a few more points because I think there's so many great pieces.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.01542923878878355, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>Databases'}, {'relevance': 0.004117074888199568, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ProgrammingLanguages'}, {'relevance': 0.0033311110455542803, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>WebDevelopment'}, {'relevance': 0.002604556269943714, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerNetworking'}, {'relevance': 0.00231458549387753, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>WebDesignAndHTML'}, {'relevance': 0.0015221722424030304, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>Browsers'}, {'relevance': 0.0012379869585856795, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>DataStorageAndWarehousing'}, {'relevance': 0.001085893134586513, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>OperatingSystems'}, {'relevance': 0.0006993541610427201, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>InternetForBeginners'}, {'relevance': 0.0006161765195429325, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 2977434, 'end': 3008060}, 'sentences_idx_start': 433, 'sentences_idx_end': 438}, {'text': "So Toby St. Clair, Smyth who we recently discussed his dissertation in Livestream 54, introduced a term or at least a phrasing, the compositional cognitive cartography. And so thinking about the compositionality of cognitive systems, and I think what you're describing here with this notion that the mappings are more general than the kind of attention mechanisms known, famously today, that those represent, like a lower dimensional special case of one kind of architecture.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.12410365790128708, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.015754573047161102, 'label': 'Science'}, {'relevance': 0.011623052880167961, 'label': 'Technology&Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.008059722371399403, 'label': 'FineArt>Design'}, {'relevance': 0.00648381095379591, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.006393822841346264, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>BrainAndNervousSystemDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.004972868133336306, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ArtsAndCrafts>DrawingAndSketching'}, {'relevance': 0.0036698649637401104, 'label': 'FineArt>DigitalArts'}, {'relevance': 0.0036170014645904303, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>VirtualReality'}, {'relevance': 0.0031049628742039204, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ContentProduction>FreelanceWriting'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 3008140, 'end': 3045208}, 'sentences_idx_start': 439, 'sentences_idx_end': 441}, {'text': 'Makes me think about how the Bayesian graph is kind of semantic in principle and can have all of these nice categorical formalisms around them. And you can even build the connector to empirical data with the presheaf and the sheaf, which may be news to even many empirical researchers doing data analysis certainly was for me. But the message passing provides a rigorous translation from whatever semantic model is proposed topologically to an implementation procedure that can be planned for and executed in linear time or at least with definable characteristics.', 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.6726481914520264, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>DataStorageAndWarehousing'}, {'relevance': 0.6319602131843567, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>Databases'}, {'relevance': 0.0021938327699899673, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ProgrammingLanguages'}, {'relevance': 0.0019708569161593914, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>3-DGraphics'}, {'relevance': 0.000548377342056483, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>Search'}, {'relevance': 0.0005184818874113262, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerNetworking'}, {'relevance': 0.0004274517123121768, 'label': 'Science'}, {'relevance': 0.00040019635343924165, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Business>BusinessI.T.'}, {'relevance': 0.00038804428186267614, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.00035167791065759957, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>MedicalTests'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 3045384, 'end': 3089412}, 'sentences_idx_start': 442, 'sentences_idx_end': 444}, {'text': "So message passing plays a really important part in going from the abstract what is possible, to the implementations of any of these actual models. And it does it in a really general way where is it accurate to say that we hope that implementation with message passing compatible generative models will kind of roll out better because we won't have some of the engineering challenges that less reusable abstractions might carry? It's hard to say. I think there's also certainly some limitations to this paradigm as well.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.8874858021736145, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ProgrammingLanguages'}, {'relevance': 0.06602773815393448, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>OperatingSystems'}, {'relevance': 0.03888183459639549, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>Databases'}, {'relevance': 0.024831317365169525, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications'}, {'relevance': 0.010173086076974869, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>DataStorageAndWarehousing'}, {'relevance': 0.006911597214639187, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.002455610316246748, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>WebDevelopment'}, {'relevance': 0.0019289926858618855, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerNetworking'}, {'relevance': 0.001340686110779643, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>WebDesignAndHTML'}, {'relevance': 0.0012205570237711072, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Robotics'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 3089476, 'end': 3132760}, 'sentences_idx_start': 445, 'sentences_idx_end': 448}, {'text': "So just kind of doing this kind of message passing, I think, as you were mentioning, one thing is that it kind of scales up quite easily, like linearly with the size of the graph, but that also come at a cost. So there's certain results showing this has limits in expressivity.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.118716761469841, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ProgrammingLanguages'}, {'relevance': 0.019994067028164864, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>Databases'}, {'relevance': 0.010361705906689167, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>WebDesignAndHTML'}, {'relevance': 0.0033304793760180473, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>WebDevelopment'}, {'relevance': 0.0015559610910713673, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>DataStorageAndWarehousing'}, {'relevance': 0.001381526468321681, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerNetworking'}, {'relevance': 0.0010958213824778795, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>Email'}, {'relevance': 0.0009705075644887984, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>OperatingSystems'}, {'relevance': 0.0008283210336230695, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>3-DGraphics'}, {'relevance': 0.0007857800810597837, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>DesktopPublishing'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 3132830, 'end': 3150060}, 'sentences_idx_start': 449, 'sentences_idx_end': 450}, {'text': "So if you actually want to go beyond this, for instance, instead of just looking at pairs of nodes, you have to look at tuples and these kind of high order groupings of nodes in order to kind of get higher explicitity. There's all sorts of techniques to do that and there's always this kind of tension between being more expressive and being efficient that will always be there in any sort of algorithm or method. It's kind of hard to say.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.04918648675084114, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ProgrammingLanguages'}, {'relevance': 0.026168545708060265, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>Databases'}, {'relevance': 0.005155869759619236, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>OperatingSystems'}, {'relevance': 0.0024020301643759012, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>DataStorageAndWarehousing'}, {'relevance': 0.0017947637243196368, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerNetworking'}, {'relevance': 0.0011717634042724967, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.00028946343809366226, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Industries>BiotechAndBiomedicalIndustry'}, {'relevance': 0.00023280843743123114, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>CloudComputing'}, {'relevance': 0.00022911140695214272, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>InformationAndNetworkSecurity'}, {'relevance': 0.00022522234939970076, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 3150640, 'end': 3188410}, 'sentences_idx_start': 451, 'sentences_idx_end': 453}, {'text': "We can definitely say this is kind of not the optimist solution. Let's say if you want to do things message passing in itself but maybe doing some sort of computations on graphs could be maybe also something that's kind of maybe missing a bit in kind of the graph ML setting. Is the context where you assume your graph is known. And you need to have some graph structure, at least a sensible way to construct it. Right.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.2958623170852661, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ProgrammingLanguages'}, {'relevance': 0.044351428747177124, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>Databases'}, {'relevance': 0.007245227228850126, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>OperatingSystems'}, {'relevance': 0.002582254819571972, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>DataStorageAndWarehousing'}, {'relevance': 0.0015333541668951511, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerNetworking'}, {'relevance': 0.0014152169460430741, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.0005216925055719912, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>Email'}, {'relevance': 0.00034831324592232704, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>3-DGraphics'}, {'relevance': 0.00027180195320397615, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.00026691699167713523, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>WebDevelopment'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 3189340, 'end': 3227944}, 'sentences_idx_start': 454, 'sentences_idx_end': 458}, {'text': "But for many kind of more I don't know, how should I phrase that? I guess for less clearly defined things like, okay, if I'm an agent doing perception in the real world or something, right? If I'm trying to create a graph of the world, what's an object, what do I create a node for? Right? If I want to have one note or object and there's some connections between objects and things like that.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.015115862712264061, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>InternetOfThings'}, {'relevance': 0.0111255