r not as kind of humans as intelligent agents, but that's kind of some interesting thing to think about. Maybe you could also well, maybe one way to solve that is also kind of stuff like soft edges and things like that. And in some way if you have attention coefficients, it's a bit like that. If an edge has a weight of 0.1 or something, it's almost like not being there but it's still kind of there.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.9846512079238892, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.004327119793742895, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Robotics'}, {'relevance': 0.002597591606900096, 'label': 'Technology&Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.0016763614257797599, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.0008677832665853202, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ParanormalPhenomena'}, {'relevance': 0.000697258859872818, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>InformationAndNetworkSecurity'}, {'relevance': 0.0004726047918666154, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>InternetOfThings'}, {'relevance': 0.0003918095608241856, 'label': 'Automotive>AutoType>DriverlessCars'}, {'relevance': 0.00030246112146414816, 'label': 'Science'}, {'relevance': 0.00029879651265218854, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ProgrammingLanguages'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 3309860, 'end': 3336392}, 'sentences_idx_start': 473, 'sentences_idx_end': 476}, {'text': "So it's a bit of a soft graph architecture. I guess at the edge level you can implement this softness but I think it's a bit harder at kind of the node level, right? Like how do you kind of model a node that's kind of there and not there? Yeah, there's just some random thoughts that's very interesting about the fuzzy object identification and kind of similarities and differences between nodes and edges even though in some ways they have some similarities too or interoperabilities too.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.006130580324679613, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerNetworkin